Unknown: Right.

01:40:18.156 --> 01:40:22.536
Kenzo: Okay. Um, is there a way for us to talk without the hobgoblin hearing or seeing us?

01:40:22.856 --> 01:40:24.016
Unknown: Yeah, we'll just say the damn word again.

01:40:24.056 --> 01:40:25.816
DM: You just say the word, and she goes away.

01:40:26.036 --> 01:40:26.056
Unknown: Yeah.

01:40:26.056 --> 01:40:28.256
DM: Now that you know her name, you can summon her whenever you want.

01:40:28.576 --> 01:40:28.596
Unknown: I

01:40:29.936 --> 01:40:30.236
Unknown: see.

01:40:34.216 --> 01:40:37.976
Kenzo: Was she in the middle of telling something to us, or were we asking her a question?

01:40:38.696 --> 01:40:40.456
DM: No, you had just told her the year.

01:40:41.076 --> 01:40:41.876
Unknown: Oh, right, right, right.

01:40:41.876 --> 01:40:42.076
Unknown: [laughs]

01:40:42.076 --> 01:40:44.876
Kenzo: And then we, we were saying all the stuff about, like them and all that.

01:40:44.896 --> 01:40:45.116
Unknown: Okay.

01:40:46.616 --> 01:40:46.856
Unknown: Um,

01:40:51.096 --> 01:40:53.396
Kenzo: Revanka, um, could you give us a moment?

01:40:53.816 --> 01:40:54.136
Unknown: We'll, we'll,

01:40:55.416 --> 01:40:57.516
Kenzo: we'll be back in just, just a second, I promise.

01:40:57.516 --> 01:41:01.016
DM: I will not give you a... [laughs] And she disappears-

01:41:01.016 --> 01:41:01.896
Unknown: [laughs]

01:41:01.896 --> 01:41:02.736
Unknown: ... mid-sentence.

01:41:04.916 --> 01:41:05.416
Unknown: Yeah. Um,

01:41:07.136 --> 01:41:07.756
Unknown: what do we do

01:41:09.376 --> 01:41:09.596
Unknown: with

01:41:13.356 --> 01:41:14.316
Unknown: Keep her in the mirror.

01:41:16.716 --> 01:41:18.116
Unknown: I feel torn.

01:41:18.116 --> 01:41:22.916
Kenzo: It feels, um, immoral to keep her trapped when we could release her.

01:41:24.956 --> 01:41:26.156
Unknown: Did you not hear what she said?

01:41:27.976 --> 01:41:31.236
Delwath: She enslaved many, many humans, and

01:41:32.856 --> 01:41:37.076
Delwath: planned or ran a small empire probably of torture and death.

01:41:38.155 --> 01:41:38.275
Unknown: Then-

01:41:38.275 --> 01:41:41.576
Delwath: I would not feel guilty about keeping her in the mirror

01:41:41.576 --> 01:41:44.036
Drikod: ... then we should execute her.

01:41:44.036 --> 01:41:44.796
Unknown: It's cruel.

01:41:46.516 --> 01:41:47.976
Unknown: She says no time has passed.

01:41:47.976 --> 01:41:48.516
Unknown: Is it cruel?

01:41:50.296 --> 01:41:50.816
Unknown: I suppose

01:41:52.496 --> 01:41:55.116
Seeker: that if no time is passing, no suffering can occur.

01:41:58.816 --> 01:42:03.516
Delwath: I think executing her seems to be a complex proposition to me.

01:42:03.516 --> 01:42:05.496
Delwath: I've fought hobgoblin wizards before.

01:42:06.196 --> 01:42:09.016
Delwath: She may be able to overpower all of us with a word.

01:42:10.796 --> 01:42:13.016
Seeker: I agree. It, it strikes me as dangerous to let her out.

01:42:15.456 --> 01:42:18.736
Delwath: It is not necessarily within our power to execute her,

01:42:20.136 --> 01:42:21.176
Unknown: even should we wish to.

01:42:24.516 --> 01:42:28.096
Kenzo: We've been very lucky that this mirror has not been accidentally destroyed while we've been gone.

01:42:30.776 --> 01:42:30.956
Unknown: Mm.

01:42:33.396 --> 01:42:34.336
Unknown: Yeah. Just imagine.

01:42:35.416 --> 01:42:37.176
Drikod: Oh my God. Sorry. Metagame.

01:42:37.636 --> 01:42:45.096
Drikod: So if we w- if someone would've knocked down Agata's mirror to get us out of it, everybody would've came out at once?

01:42:45.536 --> 01:42:49.196
Seeker: Yes. Yeah. That would've been absolute chaos if we had tried to smash it or something.

01:42:49.396 --> 01:42:51.196
Drikod: That would've been in Agata's lair of horrors.

01:42:51.236 --> 01:42:51.276
Unknown: Yep.

01:42:51.296 --> 01:42:53.116
DM: Oh, that would've been so much fun.

01:42:56.156 --> 01:42:57.156
Unknown: Very close to happening.

01:42:57.156 --> 01:42:57.836
Unknown: [laughs]

01:42:57.876 --> 01:42:59.736
Seeker: A lot, a lot would've happened very fast.

01:43:00.396 --> 01:43:02.896
Delwath: Oh my God. I think her...

01:43:05.876 --> 01:43:07.496
Unknown: This hobgoblin,

01:43:09.836 --> 01:43:11.256
Unknown: she may well be...

01:43:13.356 --> 01:43:15.136
Delwath: She may have information that we want.

01:43:15.136 --> 01:43:16.436
Unknown: She may be cooperative.

01:43:16.436 --> 01:43:17.556
Unknown: It may be, in time,

01:43:19.276 --> 01:43:22.956
Delwath: we will find she actually could be trusted or not.

01:43:23.636 --> 01:43:25.096
Unknown: But I think it is

01:43:26.976 --> 01:43:32.486
Delwath: premature to both talk of execution or release I'm fine with that

01:43:36.626 --> 01:43:37.166
Delwath: Although

01:43:38.346 --> 01:43:39.406
Delwath: even resisting,

01:43:40.286 --> 01:43:44.426
Delwath: even though she resisted Shema, I think it's hard to imagine a hobgoblin,

01:43:45.846 --> 01:43:48.246
Delwath: uh, not deserving of execution.

01:43:49.906 --> 01:43:50.906
Unknown: What an elf thing to say.

01:43:53.266 --> 01:43:55.746
Delwath: How many hobgoblins have you encountered, Kenzo?

01:43:57.066 --> 01:43:58.246
Unknown: Not as many as you, but

01:43:59.486 --> 01:44:02.026
Kenzo: I don't know. There are orcs that are farmers.

01:44:02.026 --> 01:44:04.406
Kenzo: It's all not quite as black and white to me.

01:44:05.566 --> 01:44:07.626
Seeker: Indeed. We're learning that the, the world is complex,

01:44:08.446 --> 01:44:11.386
Seeker: perhaps beyond any of our reckoning, and in ways that

01:44:12.606 --> 01:44:15.266
Seeker: have changed since the Great War.

01:44:16.406 --> 01:44:20.626
Kenzo: And is this conversation we're having right now before or after the dreamland stuff, the dream world stuff?

01:44:21.826 --> 01:44:22.266
DM: Uh,

01:44:23.666 --> 01:44:25.066
DM: that is a good question.

01:44:25.586 --> 01:44:25.906
DM: Um-

01:44:26.906 --> 01:44:27.266
Seeker: Hmm

01:44:27.266 --> 01:44:27.266
DM: ...

01:44:28.606 --> 01:44:30.726
DM: I think it would've been...

01:44:30.726 --> 01:44:32.246
DM: Well, which would you prefer?

01:44:32.246 --> 01:44:33.486
DM: It can be either, really.

01:44:37.866 --> 01:44:38.146
Unknown: Well,

01:44:38.966 --> 01:44:39.246
Unknown: uh,

01:44:41.086 --> 01:44:45.626
Kenzo: um, it's probably before, because Delwath hasn't left yet-

01:44:46.006 --> 01:44:46.746
DM: Yeah

01:44:46.746 --> 01:44:48.426
Kenzo: ... on your soul quest thing, so.

01:44:48.486 --> 01:44:54.126
DM: Right. But Delwath did his dream world, 'cause Kendrasa can only do one dream journey a night,

01:44:56.026 --> 01:44:58.086
DM: so he had to space them all out, right?

01:44:58.926 --> 01:44:58.946
DM: So-

01:44:58.966 --> 01:45:02.106
Kenzo: But, you know, like, now Delwath is like, "Hey, I'm gonna go walk out into the desert."

01:45:02.106 --> 01:45:02.786
Unknown: Has that happened yet?

01:45:03.146 --> 01:45:04.346
DM: That has not happened yet.

01:45:04.446 --> 01:45:05.946
Unknown: Okay. Okay.

01:45:05.946 --> 01:45:09.266
DM: But Kenzo's dream world journey may have already happened.

01:45:09.266 --> 01:45:10.906
DM: It's a, it doesn't really matter.

01:45:12.746 --> 01:45:12.966
Unknown: Okay.

01:45:14.126 --> 01:45:18.946
Wellby: Wellby will chime in to say, "It's not, Kenzo, that we should execute her for being a hobgoblin.

01:45:19.606 --> 01:45:21.186
Wellby: We should execute her for her crimes.

01:45:22.186 --> 01:45:24.226
Wellby: But I think Delwath makes a good point.

01:45:24.226 --> 01:45:28.326
Wellby: There's no way of knowing if we could actually do it were she to be released.

01:45:28.326 --> 01:45:31.886
Wellby: But I can't imagine a different course of action if we were to release her."

01:45:34.566 --> 01:45:35.006
Seeker: Mm-hmm.

01:45:38.426 --> 01:45:40.266
Seeker: We might nonetheless be able to

01:45:41.305 --> 01:45:43.766
Seeker: manipulate her, uh,

01:45:45.346 --> 01:45:48.046
Seeker: perhaps twisting her sense of pride, her ego,

01:45:49.086 --> 01:45:49.386
Seeker: uh-

01:45:49.546 --> 01:45:49.786
Drikod: Or-

01:45:49.786 --> 01:45:53.946
Seeker: ... giving false promises of release in order to extract

01:45:55.066 --> 01:45:57.586
Seeker: some more knowledge from her, if there's anything we need to know

01:45:57.586 --> 01:46:00.726
Drikod: ... Drikod feels bad saying this, but

01:46:01.966 --> 01:46:02.646
Drikod: you could also

01:46:03.666 --> 01:46:06.046
Drikod: create a reality for her.

01:46:06.046 --> 01:46:15.206
Drikod: She knows nothing of this world, so you can manipulate her by what falsehoods you give her, or you figure out what,

01:46:16.746 --> 01:46:19.766
Drikod: what is the political situation or the social or the,

01:46:20.906 --> 01:46:23.246
Drikod: the world that would give her incentives to tell you things.

01:46:23.646 --> 01:46:24.306
Seeker: So for example,

01:46:25.506 --> 01:46:25.806
Seeker: um,

01:46:26.646 --> 01:46:32.326
Seeker: that Sembara is in hobgoblin hands now in this comple- chaotic post-war period, and-

01:46:32.446 --> 01:46:32.666
Drikod: Mm

01:46:32.666 --> 01:46:37.246
Seeker: ... perhaps we could take the mirror there and release her to find her own fortune.

01:46:40.046 --> 01:46:40.966
Seeker: If she tells us

01:46:42.906 --> 01:46:44.766
Seeker: certain crucial facts, such as,

01:46:46.406 --> 01:46:48.146
Seeker: what do, what do we need to know? Shema's birthday.

01:46:48.186 --> 01:46:52.146
Seeker: I, uh, uh, I wonder what, what we might ask, for someone who has actually-

01:46:52.246 --> 01:46:52.706
Drikod: We should

01:46:52.706 --> 01:46:54.566
Seeker: ... mingled with Shema directly.

01:46:58.066 --> 01:46:58.646
Delwath: I think we should-

01:46:58.706 --> 01:47:00.146
Drikod: Be careful what you tell her.

01:47:01.626 --> 01:47:02.966
Delwath: Yes. I would be careful,

01:47:04.106 --> 01:47:06.206
Delwath: although I think it's hard to imagine a

01:47:07.006 --> 01:47:08.026
Delwath: escape. If,

01:47:09.426 --> 01:47:12.806
Delwath: if she has the ability to travel between planes, she would have already used it,

01:47:13.926 --> 01:47:17.706
Delwath: I presume. Without that ability, I s- do not see how she could escape.

01:47:18.506 --> 01:47:18.686
Seeker: Well-

01:47:18.726 --> 01:47:21.766
Drikod: Oh, my God. But why would she, how would she know she was trapped?

01:47:21.766 --> 01:47:24.946
Drikod: If it was just but a moment, she could still be gathering her...

01:47:25.646 --> 01:47:26.166
Drikod: She hasn't-

01:47:26.406 --> 01:47:26.546
Seeker: It, eh

01:47:26.546 --> 01:47:27.826
Drikod: ... experienced time.

01:47:27.846 --> 01:47:31.266
Drikod: Now she knows how long she has been trapped, so she may have urgency.

01:47:32.126 --> 01:47:36.226
Delwath: It, it certainly did not, being inside the mirror, it didn't

01:47:38.426 --> 01:47:38.726
Delwath: feel like-

01:47:38.746 --> 01:47:40.746
DM: It didn't feel like no time was passing

01:47:40.746 --> 01:47:41.686
Delwath: ... no time.

01:47:41.686 --> 01:47:43.366
DM: Right. Yeah.

01:47:43.366 --> 01:47:44.106
Delwath: It, it, it, it...

01:47:45.046 --> 01:47:46.566
Delwath: I was only there for a short while,

01:47:48.226 --> 01:47:50.146
Delwath: and I think there was no...

01:47:52.806 --> 01:47:58.626
Delwath: It could feel like a short mo- like a brief moment if you never get hungry or sleepy or thirsty-

01:47:59.086 --> 01:47:59.086
DM: Mm

01:47:59.086 --> 01:48:01.186
Delwath: ... and feel no need to, to,

01:48:02.566 --> 01:48:02.886
Delwath: you know,

01:48:04.946 --> 01:48:07.906
Delwath: without feeling restless or if it...

01:48:08.546 --> 01:48:12.366
Delwath: But that doesn't mean that she doesn't perceive herself as trapped.

01:48:12.366 --> 01:48:14.926
Delwath: It doesn't mean that no time has passed, right?

01:48:16.026 --> 01:48:16.106
Seeker: Look-

01:48:16.126 --> 01:48:24.006
Delwath: But certainly when I was trapped there, I felt trapped, and if had, I had the ability to have escaped, I certainly would have

01:48:25.186 --> 01:48:27.146
Kenzo: Yeah. Like, um, I think

01:48:29.566 --> 01:48:34.326
Kenzo: we can speak to her again if there's, if there are questions that emerge.

01:48:35.166 --> 01:48:37.706
Kenzo: For now, um, I agree with you all.

01:48:38.146 --> 01:48:40.506
Kenzo: Leaving her in is the best course of action.

01:48:41.386 --> 01:48:47.386
Kenzo: If she does escape, I don't think we've actually wronged her in any way, and in fact, we've demonstrated some willingness to share some truth-

01:48:47.406 --> 01:48:47.466
Delwath: Yeah

01:48:47.466 --> 01:48:51.246
Kenzo: ... about the situation. So I don't think that she'd be, we would be adversaries.

01:48:52.246 --> 01:48:59.126
Kenzo: I mean, it's true, though, that this is her grandfather's mirror, or her grandfather's mirror, so she actually may know an escape route that we're not aware of.

01:48:59.146 --> 01:48:59.706
Unknown: Who knows?

01:49:00.506 --> 01:49:01.186
Unknown: But ooh,

01:49:02.306 --> 01:49:11.226
Kenzo: my bigger concern right now is just where do we s- where do we store this thing so that, one, she doesn't pop out accidentally, and two, um,

01:49:12.626 --> 01:49:14.606
Kenzo: somebody else doesn't accidentally get sucked in there.

01:49:15.946 --> 01:49:19.606
Delwath: We did learn there's a word we can speak to turn it off.

01:49:20.266 --> 01:49:22.106
Seeker: Mm-hmm. Ugh.

01:49:22.126 --> 01:49:23.806
Seeker: We can turn it on and off at will.

01:49:24.426 --> 01:49:28.486
DM: I assume you must have done that, because otherwise you can't actually talk to somebody without all being-

01:49:28.526 --> 01:49:28.626
Delwath: Right

01:49:28.626 --> 01:49:29.546
DM: ... at risk of being sucked into the mirror.

01:49:29.546 --> 01:49:31.046
Delwath: There you go. Yes. Yes.

01:49:31.086 --> 01:49:32.806
Seeker: Yeah. So this trick we're doing-

01:49:32.846 --> 01:49:32.846
Drikod: Okay

01:49:32.846 --> 01:49:38.974
Seeker: ... is to disable its sucking you in functionality And then also bring someone to the surface on the inside

01:49:38.994 --> 01:49:40.394
Delwath: And I think we should keep it with us.

01:49:40.854 --> 01:49:42.854
Delwath: I can't think of a safer spot.

01:49:43.614 --> 01:49:44.014
Unknown: I agree.

01:49:44.394 --> 01:49:45.074
Seeker: And to be honest,

01:49:46.234 --> 01:49:49.614
Seeker: it is a reasonably po- reasonably powerful defensive asset-

01:49:49.814 --> 01:49:50.074
Unknown: Mm

01:49:50.074 --> 01:49:50.074
Seeker: ...

01:49:52.234 --> 01:49:53.934
Seeker: if we need to hold it up in front of any creature-

01:49:53.974 --> 01:49:53.974
Delwath: Mm-hmm

01:49:53.974 --> 01:49:54.734
Seeker: ... that threatens us.

01:49:55.494 --> 01:49:56.934
Delwath: Except that it weighs 50 pounds,

01:49:58.074 --> 01:49:59.454
Delwath: and it's relatively easy to break.

01:50:00.554 --> 01:50:00.914
Unknown: Mm.

01:50:04.974 --> 01:50:06.714
Kenzo: What, where is our, like, bag of holding?

01:50:06.714 --> 01:50:07.594
Unknown: Where's our bag of, like-

01:50:07.634 --> 01:50:09.474
Delwath: Yeah, we need a bag of holding.

01:50:09.834 --> 01:50:12.914
Delwath: But how... I mean, we're taking Yudomas' mirror with us.

01:50:13.534 --> 01:50:15.574
Delwath: I figure if we're carrying one mirror, why not two?

01:50:16.014 --> 01:50:16.894
Seeker: And that thing's huge, right?

01:50:18.054 --> 01:50:18.574
Delwath: Uh, that thing's-

01:50:18.574 --> 01:50:19.334
Seeker: It's a much larger mirror

01:50:19.334 --> 01:50:21.394
DM: ... taller, but it's more of a,

01:50:22.734 --> 01:50:24.054
Delwath: um... it's not as heavy.

01:50:25.214 --> 01:50:27.234
Delwath: Like, we're just gonna have a cart with two mirrors.

01:50:28.654 --> 01:50:28.814
Unknown: No, but-

01:50:28.814 --> 01:50:29.554
Delwath: I don't know. We'll see

01:50:29.554 --> 01:50:31.654
Kenzo: ... we need to protect the shit out of these mirror.

01:50:31.674 --> 01:50:33.754
Kenzo: Like, these mirrors are, like, so fucking valuable.

01:50:33.754 --> 01:50:36.114
Kenzo: Like, if anything happened to them, I would be so pissed.

01:50:36.114 --> 01:50:38.714
Kenzo: Like, these are, like, like immensely powerful mirrors.

01:50:38.714 --> 01:50:39.774
Unknown: How the fuck do we protect these?

01:50:41.154 --> 01:50:43.714
Seeker: We could build some kind of custom enclosure for them.

01:50:44.294 --> 01:50:44.754
Unknown: I think we need to-

01:50:44.754 --> 01:50:45.434
Seeker: What material would you use for that?

01:50:45.494 --> 01:50:51.614
Kenzo: I think we need to, like, triple, quadruple, like, fucking cast some, you know, abjuration magic so people don't know it is there.

01:50:52.134 --> 01:50:55.494
Kenzo: Make it so that they seem like norm- normal mirrors, not magical mirrors.

01:50:55.514 --> 01:50:58.414
Kenzo: Like, we need to, like, go pull out all the stops to, like, protect these things.

01:50:59.574 --> 01:51:00.174
Delwath: I think we should-

01:51:00.554 --> 01:51:02.634
Wellby: Disguise them as something else entirely.

01:51:03.114 --> 01:51:03.314
Unknown: Yeah.

01:51:03.354 --> 01:51:04.474
Seeker: Mm.

01:51:04.574 --> 01:51:08.654
Delwath: Um, in the interest of maybe trying to advance the plot just a teeny bit tonight.

01:51:08.694 --> 01:51:08.754
Seeker: Yes.

01:51:08.754 --> 01:51:09.854
Wellby: Thanks.

01:51:09.854 --> 01:51:11.454
Delwath: Um, I don't think we...

01:51:11.454 --> 01:51:14.834
Delwath: I mean, I'm, I don't know that we need to talk to the hobgoblin any further for right now.

01:51:14.854 --> 01:51:15.074
Unknown: I agree.

01:51:15.374 --> 01:51:15.594
Seeker: Mm.

01:51:15.614 --> 01:51:16.454
Wellby: I agree. I agree.

01:51:16.594 --> 01:51:19.254
Delwath: Um, we still haven't decided what to show the mirror.

01:51:19.534 --> 01:51:22.794
Delwath: Now that Schwartz is here, we should show the mirror something, but what?

01:51:23.694 --> 01:51:26.194
Kenzo: Lantern. What other option have I heard other than lantern?

01:51:26.454 --> 01:51:27.294
Unknown: What else is superior to lantern?

01:51:27.294 --> 01:51:28.934
Seeker: Where, where is that on the party treasure thing?

01:51:29.434 --> 01:51:30.174
Delwath: The soul lantern.

01:51:30.174 --> 01:51:30.314
Seeker: Soul lantern.

01:51:33.034 --> 01:51:35.474
Delwath: It's, like, a big paragraph about how it-

01:51:35.534 --> 01:51:35.954
Seeker: Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh

01:51:35.954 --> 01:51:38.514
Delwath: ... it's super creepy and full of, um,

01:51:39.974 --> 01:51:40.274
Delwath: uh...

01:51:41.934 --> 01:51:48.074
Delwath: When attuned to the lantern, you can use an action to trap the soul of a creature that's died within the past minute, and then, um,

01:51:48.854 --> 01:51:50.854
Delwath: you can use it to charge spells.

01:51:51.934 --> 01:51:52.554
Seeker: Oh my God.

01:51:54.374 --> 01:51:56.334
Seeker: I bite. That sounds unpleasant.

01:51:59.154 --> 01:51:59.454
Delwath: Um,

01:52:05.674 --> 01:52:06.434
Delwath: I guess I...

01:52:07.194 --> 01:52:10.254
Delwath: Does anybody n- I mean, I don't know how to destroy the lantern.

01:52:10.254 --> 01:52:12.914
Delwath: We should really bring the lantern to Kendra-

01:52:12.994 --> 01:52:13.114
Unknown: Zintra

01:52:13.114 --> 01:52:18.674
Delwath: ... and Zintra, and, and ask Zintra if she knows how to free the souls trapped in the lantern.

01:52:20.434 --> 01:52:23.474
Wellby: I, I agree. I, like, I, in a slightly meta-gamey point, like,

01:52:24.974 --> 01:52:30.214
Wellby: the lantern, showing the lantern to the mirror, and, and Zintra for that matter, might help us figure out ways to destroy it safely.

