02:35:25.294 --> 02:35:26.074
Delwath: named Severus.

02:35:27.694 --> 02:35:28.674
Unknown: That was the buyer?

02:35:29.314 --> 02:35:32.834
Delwath: The buyer of the two other books that his cousin found in the desert.

02:35:34.294 --> 02:35:35.694
Unknown: Do we know of a Ser- Severus?

02:35:36.374 --> 02:35:37.334
Unknown: That sounds familiar. No?

02:35:39.714 --> 02:35:43.014
Seeker: And, and where in the desert were the books originally found?

02:35:45.494 --> 02:35:49.074
Delwath: His cousin will be back in town around now.

02:35:49.074 --> 02:35:51.094
Delwath: He said we could talk to him, but he didn't know.

02:35:53.474 --> 02:35:54.034
Unknown: Interesting.

02:35:57.374 --> 02:35:59.214
Delwath: The other, the other story I heard,

02:36:00.194 --> 02:36:02.514
Delwath: um, was that when, um,

02:36:03.834 --> 02:36:06.934
Delwath: when Sura was, uh,

02:36:08.314 --> 02:36:08.994
Delwath: was lost,

02:36:10.254 --> 02:36:10.614
Delwath: um,

02:36:12.974 --> 02:36:13.434
Delwath: the,

02:36:17.014 --> 02:36:17.454
Delwath: um...

02:36:19.234 --> 02:36:22.894
Delwath: When she disappeared, she was traveling with the royal court.

02:36:22.894 --> 02:36:24.594
Delwath: And, uh, Mar-

02:36:25.374 --> 02:36:34.994
Delwath: Marthu, who was the, um, pre- the old, an old elder who was sort of the caretaker ruler prior to Sura's, uh,

02:36:36.134 --> 02:36:38.494
Delwath: prior to Sura being, um,

02:36:39.834 --> 02:36:41.514
Delwath: selected to, to...

02:36:41.514 --> 02:36:44.154
Delwath: Or being prepared for the throne, I guess, right?

02:36:44.174 --> 02:36:45.474
Delwath: Like, Sura was never crowned, right?

02:36:45.514 --> 02:36:46.994
DM: She was never crowned. She was like...

02:36:47.694 --> 02:36:50.194
DM: Marathu had been like, "She's my heir."

02:36:50.654 --> 02:36:50.934
Delwath: Right.

02:36:51.554 --> 02:36:52.974
DM: But she was never crowned.

02:36:53.674 --> 02:37:03.174
Delwath: He went searching for her, and was tragically killed by an, with an orc, uh, by orcs, while she was looking for Sura.

02:37:06.214 --> 02:37:08.034
Delwath: Struck me as too neat a coincidence.

02:37:09.574 --> 02:37:12.614
Delwath: Marthu was, was a, was a...

02:37:14.474 --> 02:37:24.594
Delwath: He, someone told me, someone, one of the, one of the elders in Carawa who liked to reminisce about the old days, told me Marthu did more than almost anybody to reconnect

02:37:24.594 --> 02:37:25.614
Delwath: the east and the west,

02:37:26.514 --> 02:37:31.294
Delwath: and then to, and to sort of restore the old Dunmari ways.

02:37:32.514 --> 02:37:34.214
Delwath: And Sura, uh,

02:37:35.834 --> 02:37:40.774
Delwath: was seen as being in that same tradition, the old Dun- Dunmari tradition, right?

02:37:41.734 --> 02:37:42.074
Delwath: There...

02:37:43.574 --> 02:37:50.474
Delwath: Sura disappears, and then Marthu is killed by orcs on the edge of the Garmjala Desert, where,

02:37:51.994 --> 02:37:55.694
Delwath: of course, Agata probably controls those orcs, right?

02:37:56.574 --> 02:37:58.574
Delwath: Strikes me as all part of the same plan.

02:38:01.234 --> 02:38:03.594
Kenzo: So Agata's in plot w- is in a plot with whom?

02:38:05.774 --> 02:38:22.644
Delwath: I, I would guess Agata had no particular care about what happened, but perhaps was paid or enticed with something to get rid of the traditionalists, Marthu and Sura both.

02:38:22.644 --> 02:38:24.584
Delwath: From there, Carnos was crowned, right?

02:38:25.664 --> 02:38:26.023
Delwath: And

02:38:29.124 --> 02:38:30.544
Delwath: he sent an army into the desert,

02:38:32.504 --> 02:38:36.404
Delwath: which did not succeed at any mission.

02:38:37.504 --> 02:38:45.264
Delwath: And the rumor, although many people in Caraway I think do not believe it, but the story told in the rest of Dunmore is that Sera brought it on herself.

02:38:45.604 --> 02:38:46.864
Delwath: She shouldn't have gone to the east.

02:38:47.324 --> 02:38:48.524
Delwath: It's all her fault for

02:38:49.724 --> 02:38:51.764
Delwath: going out east and stay to the west.

02:38:52.564 --> 02:39:01.164
Delwath: Whether that rumor is spread by Carnos or what people really think, or has come to be what people think because it's the story people want to hear.

02:39:08.744 --> 02:39:14.244
Kenzo: Kenzo, after, um, hearing about the Chardonian mages is like ashen.

02:39:14.244 --> 02:39:17.764
Kenzo: He's just very, very like, you know, blood drained from his face.

02:39:17.764 --> 02:39:23.644
Kenzo: Like, very, very disturbed at hearing about Chardoni- Chardonian mages in Tobra.

02:39:27.224 --> 02:39:28.404
Unknown: What are those mages doing here?

02:39:30.424 --> 02:39:32.064
Kenzo: Civil war breaking out in Dunmore.

02:39:36.744 --> 02:39:37.864
Unknown: Delwath, do you have other news to share?

02:39:41.324 --> 02:39:51.644
Delwath: No. I, I did talk about Agata with a few people who would talk to me about her, and the only thing I guess I learned is nobody here at least thinks she's a plotter.

02:39:52.424 --> 02:39:53.124
Delwath: They don't think...

02:39:54.084 --> 02:39:58.764
Delwath: Those who heard of her do not think she was the mastermind behind anything.

02:39:59.804 --> 02:40:00.324
Delwath: She was,

02:40:01.684 --> 02:40:02.504
Delwath: she was the,

02:40:03.964 --> 02:40:05.344
Delwath: the tool, not the-

02:40:05.664 --> 02:40:05.684
Unknown: Yeah

02:40:05.684 --> 02:40:06.784
Delwath: ... not the mind, right?

02:40:07.204 --> 02:40:07.244
Unknown: Yeah.

02:40:07.244 --> 02:40:09.184
Delwath: Except for strange magic.

02:40:10.064 --> 02:40:12.804
Delwath: I did hear from one, um, woman,

02:40:14.324 --> 02:40:22.404
Delwath: the rumor at least, that the only people who had ever got anything approaching a fair deal with her were those who were tr- trading unusual, strange magics.

02:40:24.464 --> 02:40:28.804
Delwath: Or powerful magic, which I guess she collected, as I think we've seen from

02:40:30.524 --> 02:40:32.143
Delwath: Delwath points kind of at the pile.

02:40:35.244 --> 02:40:35.944
Delwath: So perhaps-

02:40:36.644 --> 02:40:36.824
Unknown: We do-

02:40:36.824 --> 02:40:41.524
Delwath: ... those who wanted to do stuff, right, traded her powerful magic in exchange.

02:40:42.384 --> 02:40:42.624
Unknown: Yeah.

02:40:42.684 --> 02:40:47.364
Wellby: We do know a group scouring the deserts for powerful magic items,

02:40:48.704 --> 02:40:49.304
Wellby: who also

02:40:51.924 --> 02:40:53.084
Wellby: are now sending mages.

02:40:53.644 --> 02:40:55.644
Delwath: Two groups, 'cause think of Grash as well.

02:40:56.184 --> 02:40:57.064
Delwath: Don't forget Grash.

02:40:57.524 --> 02:40:58.124
Wellby: Oh, that's right.

02:40:58.664 --> 02:41:01.464
Delwath: Grash is also scouring Carson for powerful magic.

02:41:02.024 --> 02:41:02.544
Unknown: And us.

02:41:02.544 --> 02:41:04.624
Wellby: [laughs]

02:41:04.644 --> 02:41:05.484
Unknown: Three groups.

02:41:05.484 --> 02:41:07.664
Delwath: Three groups. [laughs]

02:41:07.664 --> 02:41:10.104
Kenzo: Who are we, who are we working for?

02:41:10.104 --> 02:41:11.724
Kenzo: Tim, we need some more menacing music.

02:41:11.724 --> 02:41:12.904
Unknown: Slight, just touch more menacing.

02:41:13.444 --> 02:41:14.984
DM: Oh yeah, I got a little bit, uh...

02:41:17.684 --> 02:41:23.764
Delwath: But otherwise, I, I spent most of my time winding up my affairs and then this, um,

02:41:25.044 --> 02:41:26.904
Delwath: this journey through the dream world and

02:41:27.944 --> 02:41:31.144
Delwath: out to the desert to reconnect with Avascar.

02:41:33.284 --> 02:41:36.684
Delwath: How about you, Kenzo, and Seeker, and others?

02:41:37.584 --> 02:41:38.224
Delwath: Learn anything?

02:41:40.144 --> 02:41:40.524
Unknown: My,

02:41:42.824 --> 02:41:44.424
Kenzo: my journey into the dream world,

02:41:46.704 --> 02:41:48.804
Kenzo: I'm still processing it, to be honest.

02:41:48.804 --> 02:41:49.064
Unknown: Um,

02:41:52.284 --> 02:41:53.764
Unknown: Delwath, the news that you bring,

02:41:54.824 --> 02:41:55.124
Unknown: and

02:41:56.484 --> 02:41:57.084
Unknown: Wellby, your

02:41:58.504 --> 02:42:00.284
Kenzo: observations about the Chardonians,

02:42:02.064 --> 02:42:02.724
Unknown: they chill me.

02:42:03.924 --> 02:42:04.924
Unknown: They chill me to the bone.

02:42:08.184 --> 02:42:12.004
Kenzo: In my vision, in my, in my journey into the dream world,

02:42:13.344 --> 02:42:15.504
Kenzo: um, as you all know, I've been

02:42:19.264 --> 02:42:22.424
Kenzo: still pondering the mystery of this, of this jade.

02:42:23.824 --> 02:42:27.624
Kenzo: Still trying to understand its connection to the events unfolding.

02:42:31.844 --> 02:42:38.724
Kenzo: I meditated on its image, on some of the other images that I'd been s- that the jade had been showing me over the years.

02:42:40.104 --> 02:42:40.403
Unknown: And

02:42:44.284 --> 02:42:44.544
Unknown: well,

02:42:48.804 --> 02:42:51.884
Kenzo: I think both the initiation that Drikod and I shared, which...

02:42:51.884 --> 02:42:52.624
Unknown: Whose details

02:42:53.784 --> 02:42:55.084
Unknown: we won't reveal in depth, but

02:42:56.464 --> 02:42:58.644
Kenzo: I saw a lot of the history of this land.

02:42:58.644 --> 02:43:00.404
Kenzo: I think amongst us we know

02:43:03.904 --> 02:43:07.864
Kenzo: that where we stand right now was once a grand elven forest.

02:43:09.364 --> 02:43:13.224
Kenzo: That what is now desert was once alive in ways that

02:43:14.524 --> 02:43:16.124
Kenzo: are hard to fathom and imagine.

02:43:16.124 --> 02:43:18.484
Kenzo: This mesa, all of the surroundings.

02:43:22.304 --> 02:43:22.524
Unknown: The,

02:43:26.344 --> 02:43:29.044
Kenzo: the exact opposite of what we see in a way now.

02:43:30.764 --> 02:43:31.384
Unknown: And Drankor,

02:43:34.924 --> 02:43:35.504
Unknown: the former,

02:43:37.364 --> 02:43:39.744
Kenzo: the former empires that ruled this land.

02:43:41.804 --> 02:43:43.544
Kenzo: And Kenzo kind of glances at the scepter.

02:43:46.684 --> 02:43:47.564
Unknown: So much power.

02:43:49.124 --> 02:43:51.464
Kenzo: And more than that, I think

02:43:52.764 --> 02:43:55.644
Kenzo: an ideology and a corruption

02:43:58.304 --> 02:44:00.884
Kenzo: of not just individuals, but of a people.

02:44:04.024 --> 02:44:05.024
Unknown: When I was in the dream world,

02:44:09.324 --> 02:44:09.384
Unknown: I...

02:44:10.684 --> 02:44:16.904
Kenzo: It's hard to believe that this could be true, but I focused my energy on my, this shard of jade.

02:44:19.244 --> 02:44:19.924
Unknown: And I think...

02:44:22.484 --> 02:44:30.544
Kenzo: It's hard to know what else it could've been, but I think I spoke to Rot.

02:44:30.544 --> 02:44:30.924
Unknown: I think

02:44:32.024 --> 02:44:35.184
Kenzo: the dream world is a place where time is

02:44:38.064 --> 02:44:40.984
Kenzo: not a proper concept, uh, not a proper construct.

02:44:42.304 --> 02:44:44.704
Kenzo: Where we are now in time

02:44:45.864 --> 02:44:52.044
Kenzo: in the dream world is not the same as other entities that traverse it, that interact with it.

02:44:53.344 --> 02:44:54.924
Kenzo: I think I was able to somehow

02:44:56.124 --> 02:44:58.644
Kenzo: conjure or, or summon a version

02:45:00.684 --> 02:45:01.904
Unknown: of this old sorcerer.

02:45:03.624 --> 02:45:03.984
Unknown: I think

02:45:07.164 --> 02:45:07.824
Unknown: at some point,

02:45:09.224 --> 02:45:11.304
Kenzo: as we've known and I've known since the mirror,

02:45:12.084 --> 02:45:13.144
Unknown: this is a piece of him,

02:45:14.224 --> 02:45:15.784
Kenzo: and there are other pieces of him.

02:45:17.004 --> 02:45:17.264
Unknown: And

02:45:20.104 --> 02:45:20.344
Unknown: when

02:45:21.604 --> 02:45:22.164
Unknown: connected,

02:45:23.144 --> 02:45:24.104
Unknown: when embodied,

02:45:24.984 --> 02:45:26.204
Unknown: much like the Heart of Shakun,

02:45:27.264 --> 02:45:33.404
Kenzo: there is a protection, a certain type of protection that that unified form

02:45:34.924 --> 02:45:35.543
Unknown: enables.

02:45:37.464 --> 02:45:43.284
Kenzo: And Delwath, the humans and the elves, our histories going back to Dran-Kor, I, I saw...

02:45:45.164 --> 02:45:52.464
Kenzo: Again, it's, it's hard to describe, but I saw these two humanoid, these figures, these, these giant, giant figures.

02:45:52.464 --> 02:45:52.744
Unknown: One,

02:45:53.644 --> 02:45:58.004
Kenzo: I think connected to the earliest humans to Kar, H-K-A-R.

02:45:59.664 --> 02:46:00.964
Unknown: Everybody here know, knows...

02:46:02.284 --> 02:46:03.664
Unknown: Uh, and this is, like, common.

02:46:04.164 --> 02:46:05.144
Unknown: Like, what we, we all know this.

02:46:05.244 --> 02:46:09.184
DM: Yeah, you would have all... Kar is, like, the birthplace of humanity.

02:46:09.904 --> 02:46:11.324
Unknown: It's a giant island that sank.

02:46:11.324 --> 02:46:13.924
DM: It's the Atlantis equivalent in Talunar.

02:46:14.584 --> 02:46:16.724
Kenzo: I forgot about the giant island. Yeah.

02:46:16.764 --> 02:46:16.784
Unknown: I,

02:46:19.004 --> 02:46:25.724
Kenzo: but I, I saw two historical, in a way, figures battling.

02:46:26.744 --> 02:46:32.364
Kenzo: Um, it wasn't a specific army or a person, but I think factions in a, in a,

02:46:33.744 --> 02:46:36.304
Kenzo: in a battle thousands of years old.

02:46:37.284 --> 02:46:37.484
Unknown: Um,

02:46:38.624 --> 02:46:41.003
Kenzo: I, I don't even know how much time, hundreds, thousands.

02:46:41.003 --> 02:46:42.304
Unknown: Uh, it's hard for me to know. But

02:46:43.464 --> 02:46:44.524
Unknown: on one side, I think

02:46:45.584 --> 02:46:46.184
Unknown: a thread

02:46:47.884 --> 02:46:52.284
Kenzo: of human purity, a thread of human superiority

02:46:53.384 --> 02:46:55.524
Kenzo: that is a part of the Dran-Korian history,

02:46:57.984 --> 02:46:58.604
Unknown: and on the other

02:47:01.284 --> 02:47:02.184
Unknown: something more

02:47:04.544 --> 02:47:07.344
Kenzo: tolerant, something more accepting of

02:47:10.484 --> 02:47:11.824
Unknown: races, ideologies.

02:47:12.444 --> 02:47:18.244
Kenzo: Another version of the vision of Dran-Kor that I think at some point in history, not in

02:47:19.644 --> 02:47:23.324
Kenzo: history for me, I think at some point Chardin represented the same.

02:47:23.324 --> 02:47:23.964
Unknown: A symbol of hope,

02:47:25.084 --> 02:47:26.104
Unknown: not a symbol of tyranny.

02:47:27.904 --> 02:47:28.784
Unknown: And somehow

02:47:30.904 --> 02:47:32.444
Kenzo: Rye and his companions

02:47:33.604 --> 02:47:33.924
Unknown: were

02:47:35.024 --> 02:47:44.264
Kenzo: involved in this struggle, were involved in trying to provide protection for all the civilization against this, this...

02:47:45.004 --> 02:47:47.284
Kenzo: I don't even know how to describe it. A fascist force.

02:47:48.844 --> 02:47:49.084
Unknown: And

02:47:52.384 --> 02:47:54.504
Kenzo: something about the destruction of,

02:47:55.904 --> 02:47:57.184
Unknown: of this jade

02:48:01.664 --> 02:48:07.704
Kenzo: broke some kind of protection, created some type of opportunity for this ideology to spread, and I'm,

02:48:09.284 --> 02:48:11.784
Kenzo: I'm deeply concerned that what we're seeing in Chardin

02:48:13.464 --> 02:48:13.684
Unknown: with

02:48:15.084 --> 02:48:18.464
Kenzo: its expanded influence, its expanded power, the search for these items,

02:48:19.504 --> 02:48:21.184
Kenzo: is somehow connected to this.

02:48:22.564 --> 02:48:22.824
Unknown: And

02:48:24.084 --> 02:48:27.904
Kenzo: again, I don't know if it was Rye or some embodiment of him, but

02:48:29.124 --> 02:48:31.724
Kenzo: I seem to be speaking to a version of him from the past.

02:48:32.464 --> 02:48:37.304
Kenzo: He had not seen these events unfold yet, the shattering of this jade.

02:48:40.024 --> 02:48:40.284
Unknown: He

02:48:42.624 --> 02:48:44.424
Kenzo: could sense that I was not from his time,

02:48:45.984 --> 02:48:47.583
Kenzo: and [laughs] I asked him,

02:48:49.744 --> 02:48:54.104
Kenzo: you know, "What possibly could have broken this jade, and what forces are, are at play?"

02:48:55.424 --> 02:48:56.824
Unknown: Um, all he could tell me was that

02:48:57.984 --> 02:49:03.264
Kenzo: there are so many other planes where, as we've already seen, terrible evil,

02:49:04.884 --> 02:49:07.784
Kenzo: unknowable, unspeakable things exist.

02:49:07.784 --> 02:49:08.984
Unknown: Very powerful things.

02:49:11.124 --> 02:49:14.564
Kenzo: And, uh, this I also found interesting, Seeker, for you

02:49:15.744 --> 02:49:19.884
Kenzo: and me, as we're both interested in trying to understand the connections of these planes.

02:49:22.584 --> 02:49:29.104
Kenzo: Rye, I think, is still with his old companion trying to map these different planes as well.

02:49:30.844 --> 02:49:31.744
Unknown: The winds are flowing.

02:49:34.444 --> 02:49:34.724
Unknown: Hmm.

02:49:35.864 --> 02:49:36.404
Unknown: They still,

02:49:37.464 --> 02:49:38.704
Unknown: they still work together.

02:49:38.704 --> 02:49:45.404
Kenzo: They still try to map the same dimensions and connections between these planes that we're s- we seek to understand ourselves.

02:49:47.184 --> 02:49:48.904
Kenzo: So he didn't know what broke it.

02:49:48.904 --> 02:49:50.304
Unknown: He doesn't know what will reunite it.

02:49:51.044 --> 02:49:52.724
Unknown: But somehow,

02:49:54.864 --> 02:49:55.144
Unknown: my

02:49:56.284 --> 02:50:00.404
Kenzo: understanding through this dream at least, there's at least four other pieces of this jade.

02:50:01.284 --> 02:50:02.204
Unknown: I have no idea where they are

02:50:03.324 --> 02:50:04.564
Unknown: in space or time.

02:50:06.404 --> 02:50:06.644
Unknown: Um,

02:50:08.404 --> 02:50:13.064
Kenzo: there may be some way in which their reunion could help.

02:50:13.064 --> 02:50:15.684
Kenzo: Rye wasn't sure, or this aspect of Rye was not sure.

02:50:16.784 --> 02:50:17.004
Unknown: But

02:50:19.124 --> 02:50:26.344
Kenzo: it seems that, to me, whatever's unfolding in Chardin has echoes of this tyranny of the past in Dran-Kor,

02:50:27.404 --> 02:50:27.724
Unknown: and

02:50:30.624 --> 02:50:31.204
Unknown: I'm chilled.

02:50:33.464 --> 02:50:42.564
Kenzo: Chardin was not- The beacon of hope that it represented once in the past.

02:50:43.864 --> 02:50:46.684
Kenzo: And I fear that what's unfolding now is a sign of

02:50:47.984 --> 02:50:48.864
Unknown: terrible things to come

02:50:49.924 --> 02:50:50.544
Unknown: from the empire.

02:50:56.404 --> 02:50:56.804
Delwath: Do we...

02:50:58.364 --> 02:51:02.984
Delwath: Did you know when the statue was broken?

02:51:02.984 --> 02:51:05.364
Delwath: Do we know when the statue was broken?

02:51:06.264 --> 02:51:09.384
Kenzo: All I know is that it was in the future from wherever,

02:51:10.284 --> 02:51:11.064
Unknown: whatever time

02:51:12.324 --> 02:51:13.264
Unknown: or place where I was.

02:51:13.824 --> 02:51:16.224
Drikod: Why don't you show it, your necklace to the mirror?

02:51:16.664 --> 02:51:17.084
Delwath: We did.

02:51:17.524 --> 02:51:17.724
Drikod: Oh.

02:51:17.764 --> 02:51:20.364
Kenzo: I have. That's how I know it's, it's a piece of him.

02:51:23.504 --> 02:51:25.164
Kenzo: I saw the destruction of Shemut

02:51:30.104 --> 02:51:30.804
Unknown: through the jade.

02:51:33.584 --> 02:51:35.184
DM: Isn't that... When did we see Demeter?

02:51:35.184 --> 02:51:36.404
Delwath: Was that when we showed that...

02:51:37.504 --> 02:51:38.204
Delwath: Was that separate?

02:51:40.264 --> 02:51:43.264
DM: You saw Demeter in the Hall of Stories.

02:51:44.004 --> 02:51:44.603
Delwath: Right.

02:51:45.604 --> 02:51:46.024
Unknown: Fuck.

02:51:47.044 --> 02:51:48.364
Unknown: So many things.

02:51:51.524 --> 02:51:58.944
