03:25:12.674 --> 03:25:14.354
Kenzo: Uh, just, you know,

03:25:15.314 --> 03:25:17.714
Kenzo: not, not now, but like-

03:25:17.814 --> 03:25:17.974
DM: Right

03:25:17.974 --> 03:25:21.834
Kenzo: ... don't want to get sucked in and drink or, you know, Denmari politics too much, but

03:25:22.994 --> 03:25:25.314
Kenzo: would be good to talk with the potential future queen.

03:25:27.334 --> 03:25:36.714
Delwath: Um, at some point, Tim, just for, we can do this over email, but just so I don't forget, Delwath does wanna take Sintra aside and ask her a bit about,

03:25:39.834 --> 03:25:40.054
Delwath: um,

03:25:41.114 --> 03:25:42.694
Delwath: just tell the same story he told-

03:25:42.874 --> 03:25:42.994
DM: Okay

03:25:42.994 --> 03:25:44.974
Delwath: ... the party and kind of get her thoughts.

03:25:45.694 --> 03:25:45.934
DM: Okay.

03:25:46.994 --> 03:25:50.154
DM: Um, I can just send you her thoughts if you want.

03:25:50.154 --> 03:25:50.334
Delwath: Yeah.

03:25:51.454 --> 03:25:51.514
DM: Um-

03:25:51.554 --> 03:25:52.894
Unknown: Oh, Se- Seeker will, um,

03:25:53.934 --> 03:25:54.394
Unknown: bring the

03:25:55.154 --> 03:25:57.514
Seeker: mechanical toy animals and play with Jimmy.

03:25:57.514 --> 03:26:00.074
Delwath: [laughs] Nice.

03:26:00.074 --> 03:26:00.594
DM: Nice.

03:26:01.794 --> 03:26:03.134
DM: She appreciates that.

03:26:03.154 --> 03:26:07.634
DM: Still, still like always, whenever she sees Seeker, she, like, runs over to you.

03:26:07.634 --> 03:26:12.654
Delwath: [laughs]

03:26:12.674 --> 03:26:17.534
DM: Um, so as the afternoon progresses into the feast, you sort of socialize.

03:26:17.534 --> 03:26:20.854
DM: You're, you know, Delwath in particular is sort of going around to everybody.

03:26:20.854 --> 03:26:26.454
DM: Elasha's, like, super excited to see you and sad that you're leaving the next day, 'cause she's barely had a chance...

03:26:26.454 --> 03:26:29.194
DM: or, or in two days, 'cause she's barely had a chance to talk to you.

03:26:29.194 --> 03:26:29.314
DM: But

03:26:30.554 --> 03:26:36.074
DM: eagerly tells you the story of the thousand miles that she's read- rode over the past month, and how she's

03:26:37.234 --> 03:26:41.554
DM: traveled from here to Toka and here to Toka, and then north and then south, and then back to Toka.

03:26:41.554 --> 03:26:43.674
DM: And now she's back here, and now

03:26:45.154 --> 03:26:47.434
DM: she's really looking forward to riding

03:26:48.814 --> 03:26:49.954
DM: somewhere else soon.

03:26:51.194 --> 03:26:56.494
DM: But is also super excited to hear your stories and, and just, you know, chatting and, and trying to

03:26:57.834 --> 03:27:03.474
DM: understand the details of all the history that you've, that you've, um, spoken to.

03:27:03.474 --> 03:27:07.154
DM: Ikrim's, you know, his usual cheerful, friendly self.

03:27:07.154 --> 03:27:11.294
DM: He's got probably the most well set table of everybody.

03:27:12.094 --> 03:27:12.294
DM: Um-

03:27:12.854 --> 03:27:14.874
Kenzo: Definitely close the night at Ikrim's table.

03:27:15.434 --> 03:27:16.734
DM: Yeah. Um-

03:27:16.734 --> 03:27:17.514
Unknown: That's the last table

03:27:19.038 --> 03:27:19.158
DM: You, you are-

03:27:19.158 --> 03:27:19.458
Unknown: Oh, and, and it's-

03:27:19.478 --> 03:27:20.458
DM: You are with-

03:27:20.458 --> 03:27:21.358
Unknown: Sorry.

03:27:21.358 --> 03:27:21.818
DM: Yeah.

03:27:21.858 --> 03:27:31.678
Kenzo: Sorry, really quick. Um, A- Alesch, too, can we like, uh, just, you know, what we were talking the last just like, you know, like what's the best way to get to Tokra, shit to avoid, da, da, da, for the journey?

03:27:31.678 --> 03:27:34.838
Kenzo: And then also, like she's probably the most recent person that knows stuff that happened there.

03:27:35.378 --> 03:27:39.318
Kenzo: And you know, again, um, you know, Kenzo was there for a while, so like-

03:27:39.438 --> 03:27:39.538
DM: Yeah

03:27:39.538 --> 03:27:42.538
Kenzo: ... Kenzo like asks her like, "Ah, what's going on with that tavern?

03:27:42.538 --> 03:27:45.418
Kenzo: What's going on with it?" You know, so kind of just tries to understand the latest.

03:27:46.238 --> 03:27:46.458
Unknown: So.

03:27:46.498 --> 03:27:46.738
DM: Okay.

03:27:47.578 --> 03:27:50.358
DM: You know, I didn't spend that much time in Tokra, actually.

03:27:50.358 --> 03:27:54.758
DM: I was riding and riding, and I would mostly just be talking to people.

03:27:54.838 --> 03:27:56.578
DM: I, it...

03:27:56.578 --> 03:27:58.678
DM: I haven't ever been in a city that big before.

03:27:58.678 --> 03:28:00.578
DM: It was so full of people.

03:28:01.258 --> 03:28:05.558
DM: Like, even the outskirts were just covered in people.

03:28:05.558 --> 03:28:08.198
DM: How do you... You lived there for five years.

03:28:08.198 --> 03:28:08.578
DM: How do you,

03:28:10.398 --> 03:28:12.118
DM: how do you handle all those people?

03:28:12.678 --> 03:28:13.638
Unknown: And what's the name of the tavern?

03:28:14.778 --> 03:28:15.558
DM: Uh,

03:28:17.598 --> 03:28:19.018
DM: I know I wrote this down. Hold on.

03:28:21.338 --> 03:28:21.438
DM: Uh.

03:28:21.498 --> 03:28:21.958
Unknown: Anyway.

03:28:28.938 --> 03:28:29.438
DM: Oh, I don't think-

03:28:29.498 --> 03:28:29.578
Unknown: It's okay

03:28:29.578 --> 03:28:30.938
DM: ... I wrote down the name of the tavern.

03:28:30.958 --> 03:28:32.358
DM: I wrote down the name of the guy.

03:28:33.018 --> 03:28:36.278
Kenzo: Yeah, just, you know, Kenzo doesn't have to be right this second, but you know-

03:28:36.318 --> 03:28:36.378
DM: Yeah, yeah

03:28:36.378 --> 03:28:37.478
Unknown: ... he'll ask about the tavern and

03:28:38.378 --> 03:28:39.278
Unknown: that he used to go to.

03:28:41.298 --> 03:28:45.338
DM: Yeah, I, I, I, I didn't go to any of those places.

03:28:45.338 --> 03:28:47.138
DM: I was always just hanging out with...

03:28:47.138 --> 03:28:48.718
DM: You know, Ikrim set up his own little,

03:28:49.738 --> 03:28:53.718
DM: uh, shop in the, in the camp where, where everybody was staying, right?

03:28:53.718 --> 03:28:55.318
DM: So it was, you know,

03:28:56.418 --> 03:28:59.518
DM: nice to see that little bit of home.

03:28:59.518 --> 03:28:59.978
DM: It was...

03:29:01.838 --> 03:29:03.338
DM: I don't know, what's...

03:29:03.338 --> 03:29:06.498
DM: Are, are cities always so chaotic?

03:29:07.198 --> 03:29:10.778
DM: Like, there were so many people there, and they weren't all people I knew.

03:29:10.778 --> 03:29:11.178
DM: They were

03:29:13.378 --> 03:29:14.598
DM: like strangers.

03:29:14.598 --> 03:29:15.958
DM: There were-

03:29:15.998 --> 03:29:16.278
Unknown: Halflings?

03:29:16.358 --> 03:29:17.498
DM: Not just Dunmari

03:29:17.518 --> 03:29:17.658
Unknown: Dwarves?

03:29:17.658 --> 03:29:19.098
DM: There were Chardonians.

03:29:19.118 --> 03:29:19.478
DM: There were,

03:29:20.958 --> 03:29:22.218
DM: there were dwarves.

03:29:22.218 --> 03:29:24.518
DM: There were, there were halflings.

03:29:24.518 --> 03:29:26.838
DM: I think I might have even seen one of

03:29:28.258 --> 03:29:29.038
DM: stoneborn.

03:29:30.878 --> 03:29:33.678
DM: And there were just people coming and going and coming and going.

03:29:35.878 --> 03:29:36.058
DM: Is this-

03:29:36.098 --> 03:29:36.658
Unknown: It's Tokra.

03:29:37.518 --> 03:29:37.878
DM: Hmm.

03:29:39.258 --> 03:29:41.258
Kenzo: Just wait till you, if you ever get to Chardin one day.

03:29:42.438 --> 03:29:43.698
DM: Oh, I, I do not want...

03:29:43.698 --> 03:29:43.898
DM: I...

03:29:44.678 --> 03:29:54.698
DM: Chardin would be very interesting because it's true that there's a lot of history there, and I would be very much like to see some of the towers, especially the oldest towers that date to the

03:29:54.698 --> 03:29:56.738
DM: founding of Chardin. But, ah,

03:29:57.818 --> 03:29:58.498
DM: it must be...

03:29:59.658 --> 03:30:00.498
DM: There must be what?

03:30:02.038 --> 03:30:03.738
DM: Millions of people who live there.

03:30:04.758 --> 03:30:04.938
DM: Ugh.

03:30:05.718 --> 03:30:09.218
DM: How could you... You couldn't even know a tiny fraction of them.

03:30:09.218 --> 03:30:11.078
DM: It's not a community.

03:30:13.178 --> 03:30:13.598
Unknown: It's an empire.

03:30:13.618 --> 03:30:14.498
DM: I would not like to go there.

03:30:16.138 --> 03:30:17.858
DM: One thing, one thing about Tokra.

03:30:17.858 --> 03:30:18.158
DM: So,

03:30:20.358 --> 03:30:20.538
DM: hmm,

03:30:22.278 --> 03:30:22.758
DM: there was

03:30:23.778 --> 03:30:27.118
DM: some rumors that somebody had snuck into the archives.

03:30:30.538 --> 03:30:31.698
Unknown: Delta sneaked in as well.

03:30:31.798 --> 03:30:32.618
DM: I was wondering about that.

03:30:32.618 --> 03:30:34.598
Kenzo: Do you know what was stolen from there, or was taken from there?

03:30:36.558 --> 03:30:41.658
DM: Well, there's a lot of pretty important documents in the archives, some say even magic.

03:30:44.638 --> 03:30:45.638
DM: Words have power.

03:30:48.958 --> 03:30:51.058
Kenzo: Kenzo kind of glances at his companions.

03:30:51.058 --> 03:30:51.278
Unknown: Um,

03:30:52.558 --> 03:30:54.418
Kenzo: I have an old friend that used to work in the archives.

03:30:54.418 --> 03:30:56.678
Kenzo: Might be able to learn a little bit more about this once we get there.

03:30:59.498 --> 03:31:02.258
DM: There were, there were lots of strange rumors there.

03:31:02.258 --> 03:31:02.718
DM: I mean, I didn't,

03:31:03.838 --> 03:31:06.678
DM: I didn't really listen to them too much.

03:31:06.678 --> 03:31:09.858
DM: You know, actually, what I should tell you about is the, is the bridge.

03:31:09.858 --> 03:31:10.938
DM: You know about the bridge?

03:31:11.978 --> 03:31:13.638
DM: It's interesting because it's not,

03:31:14.898 --> 03:31:15.318
DM: it's not

03:31:16.438 --> 03:31:18.758
DM: Drankorian. Most of the big famous

03:31:20.018 --> 03:31:23.978
DM: architectural features around here, everybody assumes they must be Drankorian.

03:31:23.978 --> 03:31:25.858
DM: But this was... We built this.

03:31:25.858 --> 03:31:27.278
DM: It's a Dunmari bridge.

03:31:28.558 --> 03:31:28.598
Unknown: Hmm.

03:31:28.618 --> 03:31:30.498
DM: But it must be 600 years old.

03:31:30.498 --> 03:31:33.238
DM: That's almost the founding of this country.

03:31:33.238 --> 03:31:35.318
DM: I was fascinated by that. And there's...

03:31:35.318 --> 03:31:38.118
DM: She looks at Seeker. You know, there's dwarven architecture there, too.

03:31:39.878 --> 03:31:40.938
DM: Have you been to Tokra?

03:31:42.238 --> 03:31:43.778
Seeker: And meta game, I have, right?

03:31:44.278 --> 03:31:44.598
DM: Yes.

03:31:45.358 --> 03:31:48.178
DM: So you would have r- Like, the gates were, the gates were made by dwarves.

03:31:48.178 --> 03:31:52.058
DM: There's been parts of Tokra that have been repaired by dwarves over the years.

03:31:53.858 --> 03:31:56.278
DM: It's fascinating how all these things blend together.

03:31:57.438 --> 03:32:00.818
DM: I'd like to learn more about the history of the dwarves at some point.

03:32:00.818 --> 03:32:04.718
DM: I mean, I've never really thought too much about them until I met you, but

03:32:06.358 --> 03:32:08.538
DM: they h- must have a really long history.

03:32:11.398 --> 03:32:15.578
Seeker: You could say we go back a long ways, and we've always been building things out of stone.

03:32:16.858 --> 03:32:20.118
DM: Fascinating. Well, I'll, I, I'm sure you have many people to talk to.

03:32:20.118 --> 03:32:22.758
DM: I'll, I'll let you get onto your next meal.

03:32:22.798 --> 03:32:25.158
DM: I, I know you can't spend the entire night with me, but

03:32:26.438 --> 03:32:27.618
DM: it's very nice catching up.

03:32:29.418 --> 03:32:32.038
Kenzo: I'm sure our paths will cross again, Alesch.

03:32:32.038 --> 03:32:32.678
DM: Indeed.

03:32:34.578 --> 03:32:35.558
Seeker: What do you think of Sera?

03:32:38.098 --> 03:32:40.098
DM: I'd heard those rumors.

03:32:40.098 --> 03:32:42.598
DM: Huvdar is quite taken.

03:32:44.278 --> 03:32:44.338
DM: I...

03:32:49.958 --> 03:32:51.478
DM: I try and stay out of politics,

03:32:53.538 --> 03:32:55.278
DM: but I can't say I'm a fan of

03:32:57.078 --> 03:32:58.138
DM: Samrat Karnoss.

03:33:02.378 --> 03:33:02.598
DM: I...

03:33:08.538 --> 03:33:10.078
DM: Dunmari should stick together.

03:33:13.218 --> 03:33:13.558
Unknown: Hear, hear.

03:33:13.558 --> 03:33:14.398
DM: Shouldn't abandon us.

03:33:16.138 --> 03:33:16.638
Unknown: Cheers to that.

03:33:16.658 --> 03:33:18.778
DM: This place is Dunmar. We've...

03:33:18.778 --> 03:33:19.158
DM: This is...

03:33:19.958 --> 03:33:23.678
DM: This, she points at the mesa, is the center, the heart of our country.

03:33:24.838 --> 03:33:29.028
DM: Cannot abandon it.

03:33:29.028 --> 03:33:29.848
DM: That is wrong.

03:33:35.048 --> 03:33:40.948
DM: But [sighs] I don't like to think about what might happen next.

03:33:46.388 --> 03:33:46.808
DM: Anyway,

03:33:48.808 --> 03:33:50.488
DM: pa- there's lots of great food.

03:33:50.488 --> 03:33:52.048
DM: You should really go check out Ikrem's table.

03:33:52.048 --> 03:33:52.288
Unknown: Sure will.

03:33:53.468 --> 03:33:55.468
DM: I'm sure he's got the best food of everybody.

03:33:57.088 --> 03:34:01.208
DM: And make sure you get a good spot before the party starts tonight, 'cause, you know,

03:34:03.168 --> 03:34:05.068
DM: he'll have the best music, he'll have the best

03:34:06.248 --> 03:34:06.908
DM: food and drink.

03:34:08.168 --> 03:34:12.388
DM: The party after the, after the feast is always the best part.

03:34:15.228 --> 03:34:15.448
DM: And that's-

03:34:15.468 --> 03:34:16.088
Unknown: Kenzo glasses

03:34:16.088 --> 03:34:16.088
DM: ...

03:34:17.968 --> 03:34:18.588
DM: heads off.

03:34:19.588 --> 03:34:20.708
Unknown: Kenzo glasses at Wellby.

03:34:21.828 --> 03:34:22.488
Unknown: You drinking tonight?

03:34:25.008 --> 03:34:26.548
Wellby: Uh, a little bit.

03:34:26.548 --> 03:34:26.968
Wellby: Little bit.

03:34:28.788 --> 03:34:32.888
Wellby: I feel like I had some bad luck last time I was at a big celebration in this town,

03:34:33.868 --> 03:34:35.088
Wellby: so I think I'm gonna take it a little easy.

03:34:38.728 --> 03:34:38.968
DM: So

03:34:40.268 --> 03:34:47.908
DM: after the meal, and, and during the meal, the, the story of Bhishma is told, the story that you've heard before that, that Kenzo in particular is,

03:34:48.728 --> 03:34:51.248
DM: and Seeker to a lesser extent, is deeply familiar with.

03:34:51.248 --> 03:34:56.348
DM: The story of how the land of Dunmore was, when the Dunmore got here, it was cursed.

03:34:56.348 --> 03:34:57.768
DM: It was ash.

03:34:57.768 --> 03:34:59.408
DM: Nothing grew.

03:34:59.408 --> 03:35:03.168
DM: And Jivaldi sacrificed herself for the people, and then Bhishma

03:35:04.508 --> 03:35:12.588
DM: prayed and sacrificed and, um, by her, by her devotion, brought Jivaldi back.

03:35:14.288 --> 03:35:14.768
DM: And then

03:35:15.668 --> 03:35:23.948
DM: she is also... This was also the story of the founding of the country, because Bish- Bhishma was the one who led them to this land.

03:35:26.368 --> 03:35:33.788
DM: So she was the one who, who led the Damari from, from far to the east in their ancestral long ago homelands

03:35:35.628 --> 03:35:37.328
DM: to this new land.

03:35:40.188 --> 03:35:45.908
DM: So this story is told in a sort of, in a sort of ritual way, but then basically as soon as the sun sets

03:35:47.908 --> 03:35:48.788
DM: comes the party.

03:35:50.168 --> 03:35:52.828
DM: So you're now hanging out at Ikrem, at Ikrem's, right?

03:35:52.828 --> 03:35:56.308
DM: There's bonfires, there's a bunch of, um, like

03:35:57.368 --> 03:36:04.428
DM: honey cake and, and various, um, traditional desserts that are served, and everybody sort of...

03:36:04.448 --> 03:36:07.088
DM: The music breaks out, everybody's dancing.

03:36:07.088 --> 03:36:08.108
DM: Um, it's been...

03:36:10.528 --> 03:36:17.828
DM: The, the Festival of Jivaldi, where you, that you, when you, around when most of you met, was

03:36:19.588 --> 03:36:26.768
DM: held at a time when the rumors of gnolls and death and war were spreading.

03:36:26.768 --> 03:36:30.168
DM: And even though now there's much uncertainty because,

03:36:33.128 --> 03:36:41.288
DM: you know, because there's... People have heard rumors about Sura and nobody really knows what's gonna happen and, and the future of Dunmore seems maybe in doubt,

03:36:43.928 --> 03:36:46.148
DM: you can tell everybody feels safe again.

03:36:47.088 --> 03:36:49.808
DM: And this is not just the usual party for...

03:36:50.708 --> 03:36:53.568
DM: You know, it's, it's sort of like a Fourth of July type thing, right?

03:36:53.568 --> 03:36:55.968
DM: It's like not just the usual party, it's also a,

03:36:58.008 --> 03:37:00.928
DM: you know, things are back the way they should be.

03:37:02.508 --> 03:37:05.428
DM: This is our community and we can, we can stay here.

03:37:06.788 --> 03:37:08.468
Kenzo: Kind of like after the 2020 election.

03:37:09.148 --> 03:37:09.868
DM: Yeah. [laughs] Yes.

03:37:09.868 --> 03:37:10.068
Unknown: [laughs]

03:37:10.068 --> 03:37:11.048
DM: Kind of like that.

03:37:12.008 --> 03:37:12.228
DM: Um,

03:37:14.988 --> 03:37:17.508
DM: so the party goes into the night.

03:37:17.508 --> 03:37:21.148
DM: The day, the second day of the festival is strictly a day of rest.

03:37:21.148 --> 03:37:21.388
DM: Like,

03:37:22.928 --> 03:37:26.628
DM: nobody travels, nobody does anything, nobody does any work.

03:37:26.628 --> 03:37:29.728
DM: People sleep. They have small family meals together.

03:37:29.728 --> 03:37:32.528
DM: They, you know, enjoy each other's company.

03:37:32.528 --> 03:37:32.748
DM: They,

03:37:33.928 --> 03:37:34.288
DM: um...

03:37:36.888 --> 03:37:42.528
DM: You know, there's often, like, music and dancing and storytelling competitions and things like that.

03:37:43.228 --> 03:37:43.448
DM: Um,

03:37:46.187 --> 03:37:48.428
DM: and so, so nothing happens the next day.

03:37:48.428 --> 03:37:50.208
DM: So no, no journeys are started.

03:37:50.208 --> 03:37:55.328
DM: You won't all leave until the, the following day, after the second day of the festival.

03:37:59.388 --> 03:38:04.968
DM: So a, a, a few, a few little things that happen here before we, um,

03:38:05.788 --> 03:38:07.168
DM: before we do goodbyes

03:38:08.748 --> 03:38:10.348
DM: and you set off on your journey.

03:38:11.528 --> 03:38:16.628
DM: The morning of the, of the second day of the festival, after the party, when,

03:38:17.928 --> 03:38:18.808
DM: um, you know,

03:38:19.948 --> 03:38:22.928
DM: the town is quiet, people aren't, aren't...

03:38:22.928 --> 03:38:25.248
DM: You know, most people aren't up yet, um,

03:38:26.188 --> 03:38:28.508
DM: one of Havdar's messengers comes

03:38:30.028 --> 03:38:31.488
DM: to wake you

03:38:33.488 --> 03:38:36.328
DM: and says, "Sura would like to speak to you for a moment.

03:38:41.328 --> 03:38:42.088
DM: Will you follow me?"

03:38:46.288 --> 03:38:51.228
DM: So Sura has not made an appearance yet, but this messenger leads you into the temple,

03:38:52.468 --> 03:38:56.568
DM: where Sura's sitting in the same conference room that you've talked to Kendresa many times.

03:39:00.948 --> 03:39:03.528
DM: Kendresa is not to be seen.

03:39:03.528 --> 03:39:03.768
DM: Um,

03:39:06.948 --> 03:39:16.768
DM: Sura is sitting there just with Havdar and with, um, two other people, um, that you recognize from around, like from Havdar's camp and things like that.

03:39:18.548 --> 03:39:31.408
DM: And she says, she looks at you all and she says, "You five are not who I would expect the heroes of Kerowit to be."

03:39:31.408 --> 03:39:36.028
DM: Only one Dunmari among you, a dwarf, a halfling, an elf, a Stoneborn.

03:39:36.948 --> 03:39:40.168
DM: It is, to say the least, an unusual set of companions.

03:39:41.768 --> 03:39:42.108
DM: But

03:39:43.728 --> 03:39:46.268
DM: you have done a great service to the Dunmari.

03:39:49.508 --> 03:39:50.648
DM: We would not be here

03:39:51.728 --> 03:39:54.008
DM: celebrating, not just for my own sake,

03:39:54.888 --> 03:39:56.448
DM: but I know what you've done for,

03:39:57.508 --> 03:39:58.608
DM: for Karawa, for,

03:40:00.208 --> 03:40:01.108
DM: for all of us,

03:40:02.028 --> 03:40:04.828
DM: all of the people here who live here, to protect them.

03:40:08.868 --> 03:40:09.628
DM: And of course,

03:40:12.728 --> 03:40:13.628
DM: you freed me.

03:40:15.988 --> 03:40:17.708
DM: And you have killed Agata.

03:40:17.708 --> 03:40:18.168
DM: These are

03:40:19.388 --> 03:40:20.748
DM: the deeds of heroes.

03:40:24.228 --> 03:40:28.968
DM: I lay no claim to your service, even you, Kenzo.

03:40:30.668 --> 03:40:30.988
DM: But

03:40:33.268 --> 03:40:34.668
DM: I believe that if you would,

03:40:38.348 --> 03:40:39.428
DM: if you would join me,

03:40:41.788 --> 03:40:43.268
DM: we could do great things together.

03:40:49.908 --> 03:40:50.468
DM: What say you?

03:40:55.228 --> 03:40:55.748
Unknown: What do you think-

03:40:57.568 --> 03:40:59.568
Seeker: What, uh- Go ahead. What, what might it mean to join you?

03:41:01.448 --> 03:41:02.868
DM: Pledge your allegiance to me.

03:41:05.648 --> 03:41:07.328
DM: Come with me across the plains,

03:41:08.448 --> 03:41:09.768
DM: help rally the Dunmari,

03:41:11.008 --> 03:41:12.528
DM: come with me west to Tokra,

03:41:15.028 --> 03:41:17.928
DM: and beyond, depending on what the gods say.

03:41:32.528 --> 03:41:35.488
Kenzo: Kenzo kind of glances around at the party.

03:41:37.988 --> 03:41:39.528
Unknown: Delwath will

03:41:41.988 --> 03:41:43.028
Unknown: step, will sort of

03:41:44.108 --> 03:41:50.588
Delwath: nod at her a bit and say, "There

03:41:52.208 --> 03:41:55.748
Delwath: are many places to go on this earth, and many

03:41:57.468 --> 03:41:58.588
Unknown: mysteries yet

03:42:02.868 --> 03:42:04.248
Unknown: to solve.

03:42:04.248 --> 03:42:07.988
Delwath: There are many things happening outside the borders of Dunmar

03:42:09.208 --> 03:42:09.888
Unknown: that may

03:42:11.408 --> 03:42:12.528
Unknown: call us to them.

03:42:15.788 --> 03:42:16.588
Unknown: I at least

03:42:17.868 --> 03:42:18.788
Unknown: wish you no

03:42:20.588 --> 03:42:21.048
Unknown: harm,

03:42:22.268 --> 03:42:23.928
Delwath: and for all I have heard,

03:42:25.568 --> 03:42:27.568
Delwath: a great injustice was done against you.

03:42:31.268 --> 03:42:32.548
Unknown: But I do not think I could

03:42:34.248 --> 03:42:35.408
Unknown: pledge to

03:42:37.408 --> 03:42:39.648
Delwath: follow you wherever your path may take you,

03:42:41.508 --> 03:42:41.988
Unknown: and

03:42:45.428 --> 03:42:46.088
Unknown: spend

03:42:47.288 --> 03:42:48.288
Unknown: all my energy

03:42:49.388 --> 03:42:50.468
Unknown: serving your goals.

03:42:51.568 --> 03:42:51.728
Unknown: That

03:42:52.868 --> 03:42:53.728
Unknown: in no way

03:42:56.348 --> 03:42:57.468
Unknown: would I wish to hinder you,

03:42:59.668 --> 03:43:04.748
Delwath: but I do not think I would feel comfortable riding under your banner when there are

03:43:06.328 --> 03:43:09.028
Delwath: further places out east,

03:43:10.208 --> 03:43:11.068
Unknown: and mysteries

03:43:14.108 --> 03:43:17.888
Delwath: that may impact many peoples, not just the Dunmari,

03:43:19.288 --> 03:43:20.468
Unknown: that I feel

03:43:22.448 --> 03:43:25.208
Delwath: we are called, or at least I am called, to solve."

03:43:26.648 --> 03:43:29.648
Seeker: Personally, I believe there is mutual aid to be found in our futures.

03:43:30.848 --> 03:43:32.468
Seeker: But we don't need to be bound together.

03:43:33.148 --> 03:43:36.308
Seeker: Perhaps there's a way that we might meet or stay in touch.

03:43:40.448 --> 03:43:43.148
Kenzo: Tim, Tim, uh, Kenza's soul sighting, um,

03:43:45.088 --> 03:43:50.547
Kenzo: Surya. Is she like, "Fuck these guys, I'm gonna go, like, hang them now," or is she like, you know?

03:43:51.628 --> 03:43:53.748
DM: No, she's, I mean, she's,

03:43:54.808 --> 03:43:58.748
DM: you know, definitely a little disappointed, but not surprised, basically-

03:43:58.788 --> 03:43:58.808
Unknown: Okay

03:43:58.808 --> 03:44:00.368
DM: ... is the sense you get.

03:44:00.368 --> 03:44:01.528
DM: She thought this was, you know...

03:44:03.368 --> 03:44:07.828
DM: Like, getting an elf to serve a Dunmari queen is a long shot no matter what.

03:44:07.828 --> 03:44:08.368
Unknown: [laughs]

03:44:08.788 --> 03:44:10.948
DM: So she wasn't, like, really expecting much.

03:44:12.728 --> 03:44:15.148
Wellby: Well- Wellby will bow and say, "Nyannsurr, our,

03:44:16.828 --> 03:44:20.088
Wellby: my deepest hope is for peace and the flourishing of this land,

03:44:21.828 --> 03:44:24.148
Wellby: a hope which I know and trust that you share.

03:44:25.748 --> 03:44:26.148
Wellby: And in that,

03:44:27.048 --> 03:44:29.408
Wellby: I'm glad and grateful to call you a friend and ally,

03:44:30.628 --> 03:44:32.908
Wellby: though I cannot accept your invitation to serve."

03:44:35.188 --> 03:44:35.728
Drikod: Drikod

03:44:37.408 --> 03:44:41.948
Drikod: says, "The Stone- Stoneborn are f- friends, and

03:44:43.888 --> 03:44:46.928
Drikod: I want to maintain these connections I've built.

03:44:48.568 --> 03:44:49.508
Drikod: But we also

03:44:50.928 --> 03:44:53.548
Drikod: stay in the mountains and stay with the mountains,

03:44:54.828 --> 03:44:57.248
Drikod: and I or my people won't travel with you."

03:45:00.148 --> 03:45:04.828
Kenzo: Kenza- That's the end ... Kenza looks at Surya and kind of looks at, uh, um, companions.

03:45:04.828 --> 03:45:06.088
Unknown: Are there, like, like, a...

03:45:06.228 --> 03:45:07.468
Unknown: Where are we? Are we, like, in a tent?

03:45:07.468 --> 03:45:08.008
Unknown: Like, what, what's going on?

03:45:08.008 --> 03:45:10.308
DM: You're in the conference room that you've spoken-

03:45:10.348 --> 03:45:10.508
Unknown: Yeah

03:45:10.508 --> 03:45:12.628
DM: ... with Kendressa in several times.

03:45:12.628 --> 03:45:13.108
Unknown: Okay, okay.

03:45:13.208 --> 03:45:14.708
DM: In the temple.

03:45:14.708 --> 03:45:14.888
DM: And it-

03:45:14.888 --> 03:45:15.088
Wellby: I just-

03:45:15.088 --> 03:45:16.808
Unknown: She looks at her

03:45:16.808 --> 03:45:18.988
Wellby: ... I, I really love this, this moment.

03:45:18.988 --> 03:45:21.108
Wellby: I'm sorry to interrupt, but, like, this moment of, like,

03:45:21.868 --> 03:45:24.008
Wellby: awkward pause for Kenzo.

03:45:24.008 --> 03:45:25.408
Wellby: [laughs]

03:45:25.648 --> 03:45:26.568
Unknown: You all go first.

03:45:26.568 --> 03:45:27.008
Wellby: [laughs]

03:45:27.028 --> 03:45:29.028
Kenzo: Um, are there, are there, like, drinks?

03:45:29.048 --> 03:45:31.228
Kenzo: There's, like, you know, like, um, like, are there refreshments?

03:45:31.248 --> 03:45:33.028
DM: There's, like, a picture of water poured, yeah.

03:45:33.288 --> 03:45:33.848
Unknown: Yeah, okay.

03:45:33.888 --> 03:45:34.548
DM: No, nothing wrong.

03:45:34.548 --> 03:45:44.608
Kenzo: So, so you know, Kenzo, a- after all of his companions have spoke, you know, Kenzo, like, um, grabs, grabs a glass and, you know, raises it to, to Surya and says,

03:45:44.608 --> 03:45:52.508
Kenzo: um- It was with great fortune that we found you and that we were able to release you,

03:45:53.348 --> 03:45:59.328
Kenzo: and that, as Wellby said, whatever injustice was served, that there's a chance for that to be righted.

03:46:00.828 --> 03:46:01.048
Unknown: Um,

03:46:02.528 --> 03:46:03.608
Unknown: like my companions,

03:46:04.648 --> 03:46:04.888
Unknown: um,

03:46:06.088 --> 03:46:11.668
Kenzo: I think you're, you're aware, uh, Surya, I'm a humble initiate of Bishtimala and, um...

03:46:13.248 --> 03:46:14.208
Unknown: Bishtimela... What's the other one?

03:46:15.808 --> 03:46:16.328
DM: Shakun.

03:46:16.828 --> 03:46:17.388
Unknown: Shakun.

03:46:17.388 --> 03:46:18.188
Unknown: [laughs]

03:46:18.188 --> 03:46:18.248
Unknown: And-

03:46:18.268 --> 03:46:19.768
Drikod: The one from three days ago.

03:46:19.768 --> 03:46:20.648
Unknown: [laughs]

03:46:20.648 --> 03:46:22.088
Unknown: It gets confusing. There's a bunch of them.

03:46:22.788 --> 03:46:23.148
Unknown: Um...

03:46:24.208 --> 03:46:26.488
Delwath: Are you really humble, though, if you're listing three gods?

03:46:26.488 --> 03:46:28.308
Unknown: [laughs]

03:46:28.388 --> 03:46:30.188
Kenzo: I mean, it's unusual, but-

03:46:30.988 --> 03:46:31.468
Unknown: It's going to the full house

03:46:31.468 --> 03:46:33.968
Kenzo: ... he, he is a, he is a, he is a humble servant.

03:46:33.968 --> 03:46:36.808
Kenzo: Um, but, but Kenzo... Anyway, so Kenzo, Kenzo completes his thought, and,

03:46:38.108 --> 03:46:38.348
Unknown: um,

03:46:42.328 --> 03:46:52.408
Kenzo: I believe, I believe that our paths will inevitably cross again, and that, um, we are friends, and indeed, as Wellby shared as well,

03:46:52.408 --> 03:46:57.968
Kenzo: um, as a Donmari, it is truly my dream to see peace in this land.

03:46:58.928 --> 03:47:00.228
Unknown: I am frightened for

03:47:01.168 --> 03:47:06.008
Kenzo: what may unfold in the coming weeks and months and maybe years ahead,

03:47:07.428 --> 03:47:08.108
Unknown: but know that,

03:47:08.928 --> 03:47:10.408
Unknown: um, indeed, peace is the goal.

03:47:11.368 --> 03:47:13.408
Kenzo: Indeed, justice is the goal.

03:47:14.408 --> 03:47:14.788
Unknown: And

03:47:18.448 --> 03:47:19.868
Unknown: Kenzo raises his glass to her.

03:47:21.728 --> 03:47:23.128
Unknown: May we all walk this path to peace.

03:47:24.928 --> 03:47:28.548
DM: She bows her head and she says, "I understand.

03:47:30.928 --> 03:47:33.748
DM: I fear it may be a long road to peace and flourishing."

03:47:38.388 --> 03:47:40.528
Kenzo: Kenzo, Ken- Kenzo bows, you know,

03:47:42.468 --> 03:47:45.948
Kenzo: as, as, as reverently as he would a politician.

03:47:46.688 --> 03:47:50.668
Delwath: Um, is there a polite way to say, "Are you gonna go start a civil war?"

03:47:50.668 --> 03:47:53.508
Kenzo: [laughs] I think we know the answer to that question.

03:47:57.308 --> 03:47:57.508
Unknown: I mean,

03:47:58.327 --> 03:48:02.948
Kenzo: you know, but Kenzo kind of like, you know, is like, "What's Hovdarr been up to, you know?"

03:48:04.968 --> 03:48:06.848
DM: Uh, Hovdarr is basically...

03:48:06.848 --> 03:48:09.188
DM: I mean, Hovdarr has sworn himself to her service.

03:48:09.188 --> 03:48:11.528
DM: Hovdarr is, like, completely taken by her.

03:48:12.048 --> 03:48:15.628
Kenzo: Actually, actually, this is something we can ask, I mean, you know, just to, to Surya.

03:48:15.628 --> 03:48:15.808
Unknown: Um,

03:48:16.888 --> 03:48:22.228
Kenzo: as you know, we do, we do ride to Tokra next, so our paths may even cross there.

03:48:23.188 --> 03:48:23.388
Unknown: Um,

03:48:25.988 --> 03:48:26.308
Unknown: again,

03:48:28.668 --> 03:48:31.408
Kenzo: we understand completely if there's discretion in your plans, but

03:48:33.668 --> 03:48:35.468
Kenzo: do you feel that there will be bloodshed soon?

03:48:39.208 --> 03:48:39.708
DM: I must

03:48:41.708 --> 03:48:45.728
DM: receive a sign from the gods before I will take up arms.

03:48:47.608 --> 03:48:49.848
DM: My destination in Tokra is not the city,

03:48:50.928 --> 03:48:51.328
DM: it is

03:48:53.128 --> 03:48:53.948
DM: the monastery.

03:48:57.328 --> 03:48:57.688
Unknown: Kenzo re-

03:48:57.688 --> 03:48:58.168
DM: Where I hope

03:49:00.428 --> 03:49:02.788
DM: some guidance may appear

03:49:03.988 --> 03:49:07.028
DM: to tell me if I am on the right course, the divine course.

03:49:10.188 --> 03:49:11.488
Unknown: Kenzo raises an eyebrow.

03:49:13.748 --> 03:49:14.908
Unknown: You seek the Lakan Monastery?

03:49:15.548 --> 03:49:16.008
DM: Indeed.

03:49:17.608 --> 03:49:18.368
DM: I know it well.

03:49:20.188 --> 03:49:20.528
Unknown: Do you?

03:49:22.848 --> 03:49:24.508
DM: I spent a year there as a young girl.

03:49:29.208 --> 03:49:29.688
Unknown: What's the...

03:49:30.548 --> 03:49:33.988
Delwath: Bishtma, the Bishtma Monastery fell before she was kidnapped, right?

03:49:34.628 --> 03:49:35.908
DM: Yeah, well before.

03:49:35.908 --> 03:49:37.248
DM: That was like 30 years ago.

03:49:38.168 --> 03:49:41.248
Kenzo: Wait, um, Tim, she would not have been there when Kenzo was there, right?

03:49:41.428 --> 03:49:44.008
DM: No, no, no, 'cause sh- Kenzo's been there for five years.

03:49:44.008 --> 03:49:45.468
DM: She was kidnapped eight years ago.

03:49:45.788 --> 03:49:46.608
Unknown: Right, okay.

03:49:46.608 --> 03:49:49.888
DM: As a young girl would have been, like, 20-ish years ago.

03:49:49.948 --> 03:49:50.748
Unknown: Got it, got it.

03:49:51.608 --> 03:49:53.348
Kenzo: Yeah. Kenzo kind of smiles.

03:49:53.348 --> 03:49:53.548
Unknown: Um,

03:49:54.768 --> 03:49:57.128
Kenzo: I s- I spent about five years there myself,

03:49:58.188 --> 03:49:59.348
Unknown: so we've walked the same halls.

03:50:01.848 --> 03:50:02.328
DM: Indeed.

03:50:03.308 --> 03:50:04.247
Unknown: When do you ride to Tokra?

03:50:06.068 --> 03:50:07.828
DM: I ride across the plains first.

03:50:10.488 --> 03:50:14.388
DM: I ride with Hovdarr and his bands to

03:50:15.888 --> 03:50:20.168
DM: gather information and quietly gauge support

03:50:21.268 --> 03:50:24.448
DM: in case bloodshed becomes necessary.

03:50:26.968 --> 03:50:33.968
DM: When I can, I will safely and quietly make my way to the monastery and seek the guidance of the gods.

03:50:35.488 --> 03:50:35.788
Unknown: We head there-

03:50:35.808 --> 03:50:39.468
DM: Wonder whether I would have an army to fight with should I need one.

03:50:41.468 --> 03:50:44.688
Kenzo: We head there soon. Um, again,

03:50:48.048 --> 03:50:48.308
Unknown: if,

03:50:50.428 --> 03:50:51.488
Unknown: if we, um...

03:50:53.888 --> 03:50:55.788
Kenzo: You know, we can send word of, of, um,

03:50:57.108 --> 03:50:58.548
Unknown: of any happenings at the monastery.

03:51:03.108 --> 03:51:07.388
DM: If you learn anything that may be of value, I would certainly appreciate that.

03:51:09.148 --> 03:51:11.368
Kenzo: How could we contact you if we needed to?

03:51:24.548 --> 03:51:30.748
DM: I cannot predict or say where I will be at any time, and indeed, my goal is to be

03:51:33.088 --> 03:51:34.108
DM: fast and

03:51:35.448 --> 03:51:36.968
DM: fly across the plains.

03:51:39.708 --> 03:51:39.828
Unknown: Tim-

03:51:39.848 --> 03:51:43.728
DM: But many who ride across these lands should know where to seek me out.

03:51:45.148 --> 03:51:45.628
Unknown: Tim, is there a-

03:51:45.628 --> 03:51:46.268
DM: And so I have a messenger.

03:51:47.188 --> 03:51:49.048
Kenzo: And is there, like, a banner of the revolution?

03:51:49.048 --> 03:51:50.788
Kenzo: Is she... Does she have, like, an insignia?

03:51:50.788 --> 03:51:52.548
Kenzo: Is there, like, a, you know, like, a...

03:51:52.548 --> 03:51:53.168
Unknown: You know what I mean? Like-

03:51:53.328 --> 03:51:58.668
DM: She hasn't raised any, any colors or any in, or any f- you know, banners yet.

03:51:59.488 --> 03:52:02.408
Kenzo: Okay. This is good. Yeah, so, so, yeah.

03:52:02.408 --> 03:52:06.644
Kenzo: Kenzo asks- We leave soon, but

03:52:07.684 --> 03:52:10.204
Kenzo: if you have an insignia, a marking, a symbol of your,

03:52:11.784 --> 03:52:12.364
Unknown: of your claim,

03:52:13.364 --> 03:52:15.024
Kenzo: perhaps you can share that with us before we go.

03:52:20.464 --> 03:52:22.184
DM: If you ride to Tokra, I am

03:52:23.624 --> 03:52:26.924
DM: reluctant for you to carry such a thing with you,

03:52:28.724 --> 03:52:31.784
DM: in case it reveals my presence before I am ready.

03:52:32.624 --> 03:52:35.024
Kenzo: Kenzo laughs, and kind of gestures at Seeker.

03:52:35.684 --> 03:52:37.864
Kenzo: We just need to look at it. We don't need to take anything with us.

03:52:40.144 --> 03:52:43.744
DM: Seek, send messages to Hovdar should you need it.

03:52:44.444 --> 03:52:46.464
DM: You know his banners, you know his colors.

03:52:48.964 --> 03:52:50.584
DM: He will ride with me.

03:52:50.604 --> 03:52:51.244
DM: We will ride,

03:52:53.304 --> 03:52:55.684
DM: we will ride under his flags for now.

03:52:58.224 --> 03:53:00.764
DM: Although, I do suggest that you

03:53:02.384 --> 03:53:05.604
DM: join me at the oasis in a few hours,

03:53:07.104 --> 03:53:08.684
DM: as I plan to say a few words.

03:53:12.264 --> 03:53:12.424
Unknown: Um,

03:53:13.404 --> 03:53:23.464
Kenzo: Seek- or, or Eric, Kenzo was kind of like, like cueing it up for you to like, you know, show her, show her h- your, your abilities of displaying emblems and runes,

03:53:24.584 --> 03:53:24.784
Unknown: um,

03:53:26.124 --> 03:53:31.464
Kenzo: in, in the hopes that she would, uh, um, you know, share a, a pictogram or something so that you would...

03:53:32.484 --> 03:53:33.604
Unknown: Anyways, you can, you know.

03:53:35.144 --> 03:53:35.584
Unknown: All right.

03:53:41.024 --> 03:53:45.744
DM: So, uh, she thanks you and, you know, acknowledges your

03:53:47.104 --> 03:53:51.104
DM: friendship, if not, you know, pl- pledges of allegiance.

03:53:52.164 --> 03:53:58.224
DM: Um, and then the other thing before her announcement is you do manage to track down this Dunmari who,

03:54:00.144 --> 03:54:04.824
DM: who is the cousin who supposedly is the one who gave, gave this guy the book.

03:54:05.644 --> 03:54:08.164
Wellby: Before we leave Nyansura, I'm gonna...

03:54:08.164 --> 03:54:18.184
Wellby: Wellby's gonna give her a, a neatly drawn map on a piece of paper of Ravenshold, both the fortress side and the

03:54:18.184 --> 03:54:21.504
Wellby: tunnel side, though not the secret entrance, uh, part of the tunnels.

03:54:22.444 --> 03:54:28.764
Wellby: Um, and say to her, um, "It may be that this is of no value,

03:54:29.624 --> 03:54:31.584
Wellby: but I hope in the decades to come,

03:54:32.844 --> 03:54:35.124
Wellby: Ravenshold guards the road north again

03:54:36.284 --> 03:54:36.744
Wellby: when it's open."

03:54:36.924 --> 03:54:38.164
DM: Indeed.

03:54:38.164 --> 03:54:38.624
DM: Thank you.

03:54:41.484 --> 03:54:41.864
Wellby: Sorry.

03:54:44.144 --> 03:54:47.544
DM: So you manage to track down this Dunmari, um, who's,

03:54:48.484 --> 03:54:51.424
DM: uh, who is the one who supposedly found these books in the desert,

03:54:52.224 --> 03:54:54.764
DM: and he's, he's, you know, he's looks kind of hung over.

03:54:54.764 --> 03:55:00.284
DM: And he's like, "Hey, I heard from my cousin you were looking for me.

03:55:02.184 --> 03:55:03.604
DM: How can, how can I help such

03:55:04.624 --> 03:55:05.444
DM: fancy people?"

03:55:08.844 --> 03:55:10.084
Unknown: Where did you find these

03:55:10.884 --> 03:55:11.584
Unknown: three books?

03:55:17.724 --> 03:55:19.144
DM: Wh- which books?

03:55:21.164 --> 03:55:23.484
Delwath: I heard there was two you sold to a Chardonian man.

03:55:26.344 --> 03:55:28.364
DM: Oh. He looks at Seeker.

03:55:29.604 --> 03:55:30.304
DM: Yes. Uh,

03:55:33.044 --> 03:55:34.324
DM: those, that book.

03:55:34.964 --> 03:55:35.784
DM: Yeah, I, I,

03:55:36.664 --> 03:55:44.384
DM: I gave it to, to my cousin and he, and he, I guess he thought, uh, it looked like the sort of thing a, a, one of your people would enjoy.

03:55:45.444 --> 03:55:46.104
DM: Is, is it...

03:55:46.924 --> 03:55:48.364
DM: Have you used it? Has it...

03:55:48.364 --> 03:55:51.764
DM: Have you written notes in it, or is it a, is it a nice journal?

03:55:53.664 --> 03:55:53.924
Unknown: Um,

03:55:54.904 --> 03:55:58.424
Seeker: it has been of great use to me indeed, and a source of much learning.

03:55:59.884 --> 03:56:02.424
Seeker: Uh, I would love to know more of whence it came.

03:56:04.584 --> 03:56:05.144
DM: Hmm.

03:56:07.884 --> 03:56:10.324
DM: I, I, you know, I, I just found them

03:56:11.664 --> 03:56:12.644
DM: out in the desert.

03:56:13.944 --> 03:56:15.624
DM: Sometimes you find weird things.

03:56:17.584 --> 03:56:19.684
Delwath: W- where out in the desert?

03:56:25.623 --> 03:56:26.324
DM: Hmm, I...

03:56:28.324 --> 03:56:28.924
Unknown: N- nearby?

03:56:30.464 --> 03:56:30.624
DM: I,

03:56:31.624 --> 03:56:36.804
DM: I, I'm not, not sure I remember exactly.

03:56:41.024 --> 03:56:41.504
DM: It was-

03:56:43.164 --> 03:56:44.104
Unknown: How long ago was this?

03:56:44.104 --> 03:56:45.144
DM: ... not, not too far out.

03:56:47.864 --> 03:56:48.524
Unknown: When was this?

03:56:49.284 --> 03:56:51.504
DM: Oh, oh, a, a, a year or two ago.

03:56:52.564 --> 03:56:53.764
DM: Not that long ago.

03:56:57.224 --> 03:56:58.804
Wellby: Have you ever found other books in the desert?

03:57:02.864 --> 03:57:04.844
DM: N- none like, nothing like this.

03:57:05.504 --> 03:57:07.424
Wellby: Have you ever found other artifacts in the desert?

03:57:09.224 --> 03:57:12.504
DM: Well, you know, I, mm, I don't actually go out there that often.

03:57:12.524 --> 03:57:16.484
DM: It, it, you know, there's not much out past Basuda.

03:57:17.424 --> 03:57:18.444
Unknown: Why were you out there?

03:57:20.124 --> 03:57:20.304
DM: What?

03:57:22.164 --> 03:57:23.164
DM: I, I'm, I'm...

03:57:26.824 --> 03:57:29.764
DM: Why do you wanna... Why are you asking me so many questions?

03:57:29.764 --> 03:57:30.024
DM: I thought

03:57:31.184 --> 03:57:32.024
DM: I, you know, I

03:57:32.864 --> 03:57:34.564
DM: did something nice for my cousin.

03:57:37.604 --> 03:57:39.164
Unknown: There are sometimes...

03:57:40.124 --> 03:57:47.904
Delwath: Delwath will, like, be very sort of, "Okay, I'm gonna explain this to you," try and be, like, sort of soothing, right?

03:57:47.904 --> 03:57:49.704
Delwath: Like, there are sometimes

03:57:51.444 --> 03:57:53.644
Delwath: dangers in these sorts of things.

03:57:53.644 --> 03:57:55.144
Delwath: We're just concerned that

03:57:56.944 --> 03:57:57.064
Unknown: the,

03:57:58.604 --> 03:58:06.664
Delwath: your cousin or, or the person he might have sold it to, or, or even Seeker perhaps, um, that possessing these things might be-

03:58:08.088 --> 03:58:11.388
Delwath: ... dangerous or, or some dangerous creature might be looking for them.

03:58:12.428 --> 03:58:17.308
Delwath: Uh, if they were agatas, for example, it would be quite concerning.

03:58:18.528 --> 03:58:20.728
DM: Um, make a persuasion check.

03:58:24.167 --> 03:58:26.308
Delwath: Yeah. Where's my character sheet go?

03:58:36.628 --> 03:58:36.808
Delwath: [laughs]

03:58:36.808 --> 03:58:37.428
DM: Says, "I...

03:58:40.707 --> 03:58:41.708
DM: You know, that was why I

03:58:43.368 --> 03:58:44.928
DM: thought maybe I should get rid of them.

03:58:46.168 --> 03:58:47.848
DM: You know things can be dangerous.

03:58:50.888 --> 03:58:51.108
DM: But

03:58:54.088 --> 03:58:54.308
DM: look,

03:58:57.528 --> 03:58:59.228
DM: I found them on a body, okay?

03:58:59.228 --> 03:59:00.188
DM: That's all I can say.

03:59:01.768 --> 03:59:02.288
DM: Been dead

03:59:03.588 --> 03:59:04.488
DM: a long time,

03:59:05.668 --> 03:59:07.108
DM: dried out, shriveled.

03:59:08.608 --> 03:59:10.468
DM: Don't even think it was a human."

03:59:15.148 --> 03:59:17.908
Seeker: And, and what became of the, the body?

03:59:17.908 --> 03:59:18.788
Seeker: Is it where you left it?

03:59:18.788 --> 03:59:21.008
DM: "Yeah.

03:59:22.268 --> 03:59:23.488
DM: That was a few years ago."

03:59:25.368 --> 03:59:26.768
Seeker: And it was out in the open, or

03:59:29.568 --> 03:59:30.768
Seeker: buried, or in a cave, or

03:59:31.988 --> 03:59:32.588
Seeker: some other structure?

03:59:32.588 --> 03:59:42.008
DM: "Can't tell anybody.

03:59:46.848 --> 03:59:47.768
DM: It was just a body.

03:59:50.188 --> 03:59:51.708
DM: I, I was just out there."

03:59:55.228 --> 03:59:57.028
Seeker: What, what can't you tell anybody?

03:59:58.508 --> 03:59:59.928
Unknown: Tim, I soul sight him.

03:59:59.928 --> 04:00:01.148
Unknown: Tell him, tell him the truth.

04:00:01.148 --> 04:00:02.668
Kenzo: Nervous. What's the deal?

04:00:02.708 --> 04:00:03.808
DM: Uh, make an insight check.

04:00:08.588 --> 04:00:10.188
DM: With advantage, 'cause of soul sight.

04:00:12.348 --> 04:00:14.068
Kenzo: Oh, plus six insight.

04:00:14.568 --> 04:00:15.148
Unknown: What could go wrong?

04:00:23.088 --> 04:00:25.848
DM: So I mean, you definitely get the sense that he's

04:00:26.888 --> 04:00:28.288
DM: nervous about something.

04:00:31.568 --> 04:00:33.008
DM: Like, he's... Like, there's...

04:00:33.008 --> 04:00:35.328
DM: Like, he's not telling you the whole truth, basically.

04:00:37.088 --> 04:00:37.088
Unknown: Uh-

04:00:37.148 --> 04:00:38.408
DM: And, and you think...

04:00:38.408 --> 04:00:46.368
DM: You get the, you get the impres- impression that his, his holdup isn't so much that he's afraid of telling you, it's that he's afraid that

04:00:49.528 --> 04:00:51.988
DM: whatever he's hiding might get out.

04:00:52.008 --> 04:00:55.228
DM: Like, he's... He doesn't want people to know what he doesn't wanna tell you.

04:01:02.448 --> 04:01:07.128
Wellby: We can promise not to pass this information on to anyone else,

04:01:08.068 --> 04:01:11.348
Wellby: nor reveal your role in any of it.

04:01:11.828 --> 04:01:15.308
Seeker: We're not from around here, obviously, and we're leaving,

04:01:16.348 --> 04:01:17.288
Seeker: so we won't tell anybody.

04:01:17.868 --> 04:01:20.248
Wellby: What you did, good, bad, or indifferent, is of

04:01:21.348 --> 04:01:25.288
Wellby: little concern to us compared with understanding these artifacts.

04:01:26.568 --> 04:01:29.468
Kenzo: So really quickly, um, Kenzo has Sense the Truth.

04:01:29.468 --> 04:01:32.228
Kenzo: "You can sense the truth of a story someone tells about their own past.

04:01:32.748 --> 04:01:37.848
Kenzo: If they succeed on a charisma saving throw, you get a general sense of the accuracy of the story, but no details.

04:01:37.848 --> 04:01:41.648
Kenzo: If they fail, you can sense exactly which parts are embellished or false."

04:01:42.408 --> 04:01:42.948
DM: Okay.

04:01:44.088 --> 04:01:44.348
Seeker: Nice.

04:01:44.388 --> 04:01:51.868
Kenzo: So, so we can ask him something in a way that will make him say some stuff, and then we can figure out what about it is false or true.

04:01:53.768 --> 04:01:54.928
Unknown: I'll spend a ki on that, Tim.

04:01:55.188 --> 04:01:55.248
DM: Okay.

04:01:55.248 --> 04:01:56.128
Unknown: I will Sense the Truth.

04:01:57.368 --> 04:01:57.908
DM: Got it.

04:02:00.828 --> 04:02:01.428
DM: So he...

04:02:02.328 --> 04:02:03.688
DM: You're leaving? Where are you going?

04:02:07.808 --> 04:02:07.888
Delwath: Uh-

04:02:07.928 --> 04:02:11.188
Delwath: Tokra at first, and then possibly further afield.

04:02:15.188 --> 04:02:15.428
DM: Um,

04:02:16.408 --> 04:02:20.788
DM: make a, make another persuasion check with advantage.

04:02:21.768 --> 04:02:24.988
DM: Where... Or two people roll, or one person rolls with advantage.

04:02:27.188 --> 04:02:28.928
Kenzo: Who's got good persuasion? Oh, Delwath does.

04:02:28.928 --> 04:02:30.408
Delwath: Delwath has plus seven.

04:02:30.788 --> 04:02:31.128
Unknown: Done.

04:02:31.128 --> 04:02:31.988
DM: [laughs]

04:02:31.988 --> 04:02:33.428
Unknown: Let's just stop there.

04:02:33.748 --> 04:02:35.928
Delwath: 26 is... Oh, there we go.

04:02:35.928 --> 04:02:36.848
Delwath: Not as good, but.

04:02:36.848 --> 04:02:38.328
DM: He says, "Okay, look."

04:02:39.768 --> 04:02:42.768
Unknown: [laughs]

04:02:42.768 --> 04:02:45.288
DM: "I can see that none of you are from around here, and...

04:02:45.888 --> 04:02:49.008
DM: If... Except you, but I trust you.

04:02:49.008 --> 04:02:49.848
DM: And if you're leaving,

04:02:51.008 --> 04:02:51.768
DM: that's fine.

04:02:56.108 --> 04:02:57.248
DM: If you go out in the desert,

04:02:59.928 --> 04:03:01.148
DM: you'll often find

04:03:02.628 --> 04:03:05.608
DM: little trinkets, little bits of magic, little

04:03:06.968 --> 04:03:08.408
DM: things left behind,

04:03:10.788 --> 04:03:12.808
DM: and there's plenty of people who buy those.

04:03:15.128 --> 04:03:18.488
DM: People around town want little bits of magic.

04:03:19.508 --> 04:03:21.808
DM: Some- sometimes the halflings coming through.

04:03:23.728 --> 04:03:24.008
DM: It's...

04:03:27.408 --> 04:03:28.208
DM: I'm not always

04:03:29.888 --> 04:03:31.608
DM: proud of selling our history,

04:03:35.188 --> 04:03:36.648
DM: but everybody's gotta eat, right?

04:03:39.688 --> 04:03:42.848
DM: So I've been going out there every now and then.

04:03:45.028 --> 04:03:45.888
DM: Go for a week.

04:03:47.188 --> 04:03:51.948
DM: It's pretty dangerous to go too far past Basuda, as you get into the real wildlands.

04:03:54.248 --> 04:03:57.208
DM: But if you go only a few days, sometimes you find some good stuff.

04:04:00.888 --> 04:04:04.388
DM: Maybe a year or two ago, I remember this clearly, because

04:04:06.388 --> 04:04:14.420
DM: this was not... This was the first time I had found a dead body."

04:04:14.420 --> 04:04:18.960
DM: And [sighs] I think it was an orc,

04:04:22.160 --> 04:04:24.480
DM: but it was old

04:04:27.200 --> 04:04:27.460
DM: and

04:04:29.560 --> 04:04:30.300
DM: shriveled,

04:04:31.060 --> 04:04:32.180
DM: skin dried up.

04:04:34.620 --> 04:04:35.220
DM: I don't know if it

04:04:36.500 --> 04:04:37.920
DM: was old when it died,

04:04:41.440 --> 04:04:42.620
DM: but it had been coming from

04:04:43.740 --> 04:04:46.800
DM: somewhere. It looked like it had been shot down running,

04:04:49.660 --> 04:04:51.800
DM: and everything was looted but these books.

04:04:51.800 --> 04:04:56.380
DM: [coughs] What was particularly strange about this

04:04:57.860 --> 04:04:58.220
DM: is I...

04:05:02.400 --> 04:05:11.980
DM: The books themselves, the, the man was wearing on his, on his belt a, a pouch that had fallen underneath him as he died.

04:05:13.140 --> 04:05:14.980
DM: And, and the books were...

04:05:16.200 --> 04:05:25.700
DM: It looks like the pouch had ripped, and there was a big hole in his stomach, and the books were scattered underneath the ripped pouch.

04:05:25.720 --> 04:05:27.060
DM: Never seen anything like it.

04:05:31.100 --> 04:05:35.200
DM: It's like the pouch had exploded and spewed out books.

04:05:36.140 --> 04:05:36.580
Unknown: Holding.

04:05:39.400 --> 04:05:40.000
Delwath: Bag of holding?

04:05:40.400 --> 04:05:41.440
Unknown: Bag of holding.

04:05:41.440 --> 04:05:42.620
Delwath: Destroyed bag of holding.

04:05:43.040 --> 04:05:43.440
Unknown: Fuck.

04:05:43.800 --> 04:05:44.700
Delwath: Can we repair it?

04:05:44.700 --> 04:05:46.940
DM: [laughs]

04:05:46.960 --> 04:05:48.900
Delwath: It's okay if it only works for mirrors.

04:05:48.900 --> 04:05:50.760
Delwath: We just want a bag of mirror holding.

04:05:50.760 --> 04:05:51.020
Delwath: [laughs]

04:05:51.020 --> 04:05:58.240
Unknown: Yes. [laughs]

04:05:58.240 --> 04:05:59.960
DM: So I took these.

04:06:02.480 --> 04:06:03.200
DM: There were two

04:06:05.580 --> 04:06:10.460
DM: ancient, ancient books written in some strange language I had never seen before.

04:06:12.100 --> 04:06:14.240
DM: And when this Trogonian

04:06:15.320 --> 04:06:20.180
DM: professor or something s- told me he, he worked at a library,

04:06:22.760 --> 04:06:24.500
DM: was in town for the festival,

04:06:26.660 --> 04:06:28.560
DM: at the market I, I sold them to him.

04:06:28.560 --> 04:06:32.040
DM: I, I got a great price.

04:06:32.040 --> 04:06:35.220
DM: But this, this other one I gave to you was blank, or I gave to my cousin.

04:06:36.040 --> 04:06:38.780
DM: It's like, "Eh, nobody's gonna want a blank book.

04:06:40.000 --> 04:06:42.200
DM: It's, eh, it's not worth much."

04:06:43.280 --> 04:06:43.640
DM: So,

04:06:44.840 --> 04:06:46.880
DM: you know, we were all grateful for what you did,

04:06:47.960 --> 04:06:49.140
DM: stopping those hyenas.

04:06:51.000 --> 04:06:51.380
DM: Figured

04:06:53.380 --> 04:06:56.020
DM: you can have a blank book. I'll keep the money for the

04:06:57.220 --> 04:06:57.980
DM: written ones.

04:07:00.120 --> 04:07:03.160
DM: And that, that guy, I think he went with all the refugees to Tokra.

04:07:03.540 --> 04:07:05.420
DM: Then from there, I don't know.

04:07:05.420 --> 04:07:06.400
DM: Maybe he's still there.

04:07:11.500 --> 04:07:12.580
DM: But that's all I can say.

04:07:14.460 --> 04:07:15.880
Wellby: What was his name? What'd he look like?

04:07:16.900 --> 04:07:19.300
DM: Severus. He was an old dude.

04:07:19.300 --> 04:07:21.460
DM: Robes, scraggly white beard,

04:07:23.200 --> 04:07:23.400
DM: uh,

04:07:26.040 --> 04:07:29.140
DM: gray eyes, wrinkled skin.

04:07:29.140 --> 04:07:31.560
DM: Had, had all his teeth.

04:07:33.040 --> 04:07:36.580
DM: Seemed pretty healthy and spry for his, for how old he was.

04:07:42.720 --> 04:07:43.120
DM: But, uh,

04:07:44.460 --> 04:07:46.380
DM: yeah, he was very excited to find these books.

04:07:47.840 --> 04:07:48.360
DM: Said he was

04:07:50.100 --> 04:07:52.780
DM: collecting records of history

04:07:54.660 --> 04:07:56.620
DM: for some great library.

04:07:57.920 --> 04:08:00.580
DM: It's like, "Whatever, dude, just give me the money.

04:08:06.840 --> 04:08:07.600
DM: And please, don't,

04:08:09.560 --> 04:08:10.800
DM: don't spread this around."

04:08:24.680 --> 04:08:24.720
Wellby: Mm-hmm.

04:08:24.720 --> 04:08:25.320
DM: Anything else?

04:08:27.620 --> 04:08:27.860
DM: Okay.

04:08:30.100 --> 04:08:31.940
DM: So he goes off. Um,

04:08:33.539 --> 04:08:35.340
DM: as the day comes to a close,

04:08:36.660 --> 04:08:38.760
DM: uh, the festival wraps up.

04:08:38.760 --> 04:08:43.120
DM: You all, um, begin to get ready for your

04:08:44.180 --> 04:08:45.620
DM: respective journeys.

04:08:47.280 --> 04:08:47.420
DM: Um,

04:08:50.060 --> 04:08:51.920
DM: as you're all planning on leaving in the morning,

04:08:57.500 --> 04:08:58.620
DM: Sura emerges,

04:09:01.820 --> 04:09:03.480
DM: and she, um...

04:09:08.620 --> 04:09:10.860
DM: Uh, there's a commotion, right?

04:09:10.860 --> 04:09:15.920
DM: As she sort of steps out of the temple and, and people have been gathering near the oasis.

04:09:15.920 --> 04:09:17.880
DM: But, you know, as she, um,

04:09:20.100 --> 04:09:24.280
DM: you know, as she sort of makes, makes her appearance standing on the steps of this temple, like,

04:09:25.740 --> 04:09:27.620
DM: news travels like wildfire.

04:09:27.620 --> 04:09:30.880
DM: And there's been, there have been rumors before, um,

04:09:33.420 --> 04:09:35.940
DM: but... So, so people were sort of prepared.

04:09:35.940 --> 04:09:38.460
DM: But this is the first, like, public appearance she's made.

04:09:40.820 --> 04:09:47.640
DM: And she, she, you know, as p- as the crowds are gathering, she, she starts this p- speech about, um, you know,

04:09:49.160 --> 04:09:54.220
DM: Greater Dunmar, about, about the people united, about, you know, the,

04:09:56.100 --> 04:09:58.520
DM: how this is the beginning of a new era, how

04:09:59.500 --> 04:10:03.960
DM: the evil works of the fae creature, Gata Dustmother, trouble us no longer,

04:10:05.200 --> 04:10:07.920
DM: thanks to the brave heroes who came to our rescue.

04:10:10.300 --> 04:10:17.028
DM: Yet the long shadow of her evil will lies on the land still.

04:10:17.028 --> 04:10:19.228
DM: She stole the future that we should have had,

04:10:20.068 --> 04:10:25.048
DM: of a united people east and west, of a Dunmar greater than the sum of its parts.

04:10:28.928 --> 04:10:31.308
DM: I will not let her steal this future forever.

04:10:33.328 --> 04:10:34.128
DM: God's willing,

04:10:35.488 --> 04:10:37.968
DM: I intend to reclaim this future for us.

04:10:39.348 --> 04:10:40.228
DM: Who is with me?

04:10:41.308 --> 04:10:44.888
DM: There's like a big, like everybody's excited, lots of people yelling, "Yes."

04:10:45.708 --> 04:10:45.928
DM: Um,

04:10:50.648 --> 04:10:52.648
DM: and as she finishes the speech,

04:10:53.688 --> 04:11:00.868
DM: um, you can see, you know, people starting to like file forward, and, and Hovdahr's standing there next to her, um, uh,

04:11:03.108 --> 04:11:05.088
DM: now with the sword that you gave him.

04:11:07.028 --> 04:11:07.268
DM: Um,

04:11:08.508 --> 04:11:10.068
DM: and, uh,

04:11:12.368 --> 04:11:13.088
DM: you know, there's a,

04:11:14.248 --> 04:11:16.428
DM: there's a crowd that immediately starts to gather.

04:11:16.428 --> 04:11:22.648
DM: It seems like most of the people in Carowa are pretty excited about this and, and, you know, are, are moving to,

04:11:24.328 --> 04:11:24.428
DM: uh,

04:11:25.988 --> 04:11:31.328
DM: s- if not m- mostly to swear themselves into her service, but many who are not warriors to,

04:11:32.268 --> 04:11:37.488
DM: you know, just to acknowledge her and, and give thanks and, and welcome her back and, and give her their support.

04:11:40.808 --> 04:11:43.208
DM: And as this scene is, is going on,

04:11:45.048 --> 04:11:48.128
DM: um, you quietly slip out to

04:11:49.208 --> 04:11:54.368
DM: say goodbye to Kendrosa before leaving first thing in the morning.

04:12:00.108 --> 04:12:01.228
DM: And Kendrosa is...

04:12:02.708 --> 04:12:03.388
DM: He is...

04:12:04.908 --> 04:12:06.748
DM: You've never seen him looking quite so

04:12:07.868 --> 04:12:09.308
DM: relaxed and happy.

04:12:11.748 --> 04:12:14.568
DM: You know, the entire time you've known him, mostly he's been

04:12:16.028 --> 04:12:18.168
DM: consumed by worry and doubt.

04:12:20.348 --> 04:12:30.168
DM: And he says to you all as you, as you sort of come into the temple or he comes around the side to say goodbye to you while Sura is talking to all the people, "You know, I am

04:12:31.188 --> 04:12:33.708
DM: grateful beyond words for what you have done.

04:12:39.668 --> 04:12:42.188
DM: I never imagined

04:12:45.028 --> 04:12:46.108
DM: that we could have

04:12:47.528 --> 04:12:48.428
DM: Carowa back,

04:12:52.848 --> 04:12:54.228
DM: that we could have Shakun back.

04:12:58.188 --> 04:12:58.328
DM: I...

04:13:01.608 --> 04:13:02.948
DM: It's all thanks to you.

04:13:02.948 --> 04:13:03.628
DM: Here, let me..."

04:13:04.808 --> 04:13:06.008
DM: And he takes out, um,

04:13:08.088 --> 04:13:16.488
DM: like, a bunch of these, like, little vials of, of the various muds and potions that he makes, and he gives you each another red healing mud,

04:13:18.828 --> 04:13:21.068
DM: one potion of r- necrotic resistance,

04:13:22.748 --> 04:13:25.288
DM: so somebody can take that, and an elixir of health,

04:13:27.068 --> 04:13:34.028
DM: which cures any poison, disease, like blindness, deafness, paralyzation, anything like that.

04:13:34.888 --> 04:13:35.788
Unknown: Wellby does.

04:13:36.808 --> 04:13:37.148
DM: He says,

04:13:38.448 --> 04:13:42.508
DM: "This is all we could make since the Heart's been back, but please take it.

04:13:42.508 --> 04:13:42.848
DM: I am...

04:13:44.708 --> 04:13:47.608
DM: I know that Hovdahr, I know that Sura will want

04:13:49.008 --> 04:13:51.188
DM: aid in whatever is to come, but

04:13:54.808 --> 04:13:56.188
DM: we would not be here without you."

04:13:59.288 --> 04:13:59.608
Unknown: We are grateful.

04:13:59.608 --> 04:14:03.348
DM: "And I am sure that your adventures will carry you to

04:14:04.708 --> 04:14:07.328
DM: dark places in the future where such things may be,

04:14:11.488 --> 04:14:12.228
DM: may be needed.

04:14:15.368 --> 04:14:17.188
DM: So with my gratitude, please."

04:14:20.588 --> 04:14:24.888
Seeker: The fruits of Shakun's garden carry more meaning than simple healing salves.

04:14:26.648 --> 04:14:27.268
DM: Indeed.

04:14:28.628 --> 04:14:33.228
DM: And I hope over the past week I have finally been able to

04:14:34.748 --> 04:14:36.048
DM: show those of you who

04:14:38.028 --> 04:14:39.368
DM: came here seeking,

04:14:41.048 --> 04:14:45.028
DM: seeking answers to dreams and visions and mysteries

04:14:48.488 --> 04:14:53.188
DM: at least some clue that points you in a direction that may be of use.

04:14:54.928 --> 04:14:56.468
DM: I know when you arrived I was,

04:14:58.488 --> 04:14:59.328
DM: I was of little

04:15:00.348 --> 04:15:01.268
DM: value to you.

04:15:04.448 --> 04:15:07.168
DM: But now with my power restored,

04:15:09.428 --> 04:15:10.948
DM: I hope my guidance has proved

04:15:13.848 --> 04:15:15.208
DM: not worthless.

04:15:17.728 --> 04:15:20.688
Kenzo: Kendrosa, one last question for you before we depart.

04:15:21.488 --> 04:15:23.268
Kenzo: The dreams that you showed us, they were

04:15:25.428 --> 04:15:26.008
Unknown: powerful.

04:15:28.428 --> 04:15:30.888
Kenzo: Is there a way to access the dream world without your staff?

04:15:31.968 --> 04:15:32.648
Unknown: Can one do it

04:15:34.768 --> 04:15:36.988
Kenzo: alone without benefit from

04:15:38.308 --> 04:15:38.948
Unknown: artifacts?

04:15:39.948 --> 04:15:41.148
DM: I have never found a way,

04:15:43.028 --> 04:15:44.028
DM: but that magic is not,

04:15:45.488 --> 04:15:46.528
DM: is not my skill.

04:15:50.168 --> 04:15:52.948
Kenzo: How did you come upon the staff, if you don't mind me asking?

04:15:57.408 --> 04:15:59.268
DM: The staff has been passed down among the

04:16:00.368 --> 04:16:02.848
DM: Speakers of Shakun for many generations.

04:16:05.788 --> 04:16:09.128
DM: I do not know where it came from originally, although I,

04:16:11.188 --> 04:16:12.648
DM: I suspect sometimes

04:16:14.368 --> 04:16:16.688
DM: it perhaps, like many...

04:16:17.448 --> 04:16:20.468
DM: He waves his hands at the potions that he's just given you.

04:16:21.688 --> 04:16:25.852
DM: Like many other magic, grew out of the- ...

04:16:25.852 --> 04:16:28.812
DM: heart of Shakun and out of this mesa itself.

04:16:30.732 --> 04:16:35.332
DM: Do not know the story of how the first speaker found it.

04:16:36.232 --> 04:16:37.232
DM: That was never shared.

04:16:40.372 --> 04:16:40.592
Unknown: Um

04:16:40.592 --> 04:16:42.032
DM: Perhaps someday I'll learn.

04:16:42.912 --> 04:16:45.372
Kenzo: Metagame, do we have another charge in that mirror?

04:16:46.192 --> 04:16:47.552
DM: Like, in a few days.

04:16:50.852 --> 04:16:52.312
DM: You're gonna hang around for a few days?

04:16:54.492 --> 04:16:54.652
Unknown: No.

04:16:54.812 --> 04:16:55.172
DM: Good.

04:16:55.832 --> 04:16:58.352
Kenzo: I mean, I kind of want to know the story of the staff.

04:17:01.292 --> 04:17:01.432
Unknown: No?

04:17:01.512 --> 04:17:02.652
Seeker: It would be interesting.

04:17:04.472 --> 04:17:05.412
Delwath: Would be interesting.

04:17:07.292 --> 04:17:08.372
Delwath: I think we should just go, though.

04:17:11.452 --> 04:17:15.032
Wellby: Wellby's itchy to get going, but I'll defer to the will of the group.

04:17:17.972 --> 04:17:27.752
Kenzo: Uh, I mean, from a player perspective, you know, if it doesn't cost us any additional time, we could do it at the start of the next session and just,

04:17:28.812 --> 04:17:29.692
Unknown: you know, and then we

04:17:29.692 --> 04:17:29.832
Seeker: There's always

04:17:29.832 --> 04:17:30.731
Unknown: ... get right to that.

04:17:30.731 --> 04:17:31.872
Seeker: There's always murder theft.

04:17:31.872 --> 04:17:34.772
DM: [laughs]

04:17:34.792 --> 04:17:38.092
Wellby: I also think, though, that we should get to Tokra

04:17:38.952 --> 04:17:40.432
Drikod: well in advance of Sura.

04:17:40.852 --> 04:17:41.952
Unknown: No, we are. We are. She's doing other shit.

04:17:42.012 --> 04:17:44.232
Wellby: All hell is gonna break loose by the time she gets there.

04:17:44.272 --> 04:17:46.052
Kenzo: No, but she's doing other shit. She's doing other shit.

04:17:47.152 --> 04:17:48.432
Delwath: I, I think we should just go

04:17:48.432 --> 04:17:48.552
Unknown: So, like, her-

04:17:48.552 --> 04:17:49.292
Delwath: I don't... Yeah.

04:17:49.332 --> 04:17:55.272
Wellby: Yeah. I mean, her idea to, like, wander through the country quietly is, like, she just announced herself.

04:17:55.272 --> 04:17:56.772
Wellby: Like, Tokra already knows

04:17:56.792 --> 04:17:56.812
Delwath: Mm-hmm

04:17:56.812 --> 04:17:57.692
Drikod: ... that she's here.

04:17:58.052 --> 04:17:59.312
Delwath: Yeah. She's...

04:18:00.172 --> 04:18:00.312
Delwath: All right.

04:18:00.312 --> 04:18:02.412
DM: She's not really wandering through the quiet country.

04:18:02.432 --> 04:18:05.212
DM: Like, she's trying to raise an army before she

04:18:06.212 --> 04:18:06.232
Drikod: Yeah

04:18:06.232 --> 04:18:07.552
DM: ... risks getting caught.

04:18:07.932 --> 04:18:08.072
Delwath: But, but-

04:18:08.092 --> 04:18:09.992
Seeker: She's c- she's canvassing, basically.

04:18:10.072 --> 04:18:10.432
DM: Yeah.

04:18:10.492 --> 04:18:11.312
Unknown: Yeah.

04:18:11.372 --> 04:18:13.612
Delwath: It... There's gonna be rumors flying all over Tokra

04:18:13.612 --> 04:18:13.672
DM: Yes

04:18:13.672 --> 04:18:15.312
Delwath: ... even by the time we get there, right?

04:18:15.372 --> 04:18:15.692
DM: Yes.

04:18:16.712 --> 04:18:18.992
Delwath: She's not gonna be well hidden.

04:18:19.532 --> 04:18:19.812
DM: Yes.

04:18:20.152 --> 04:18:24.332
Delwath: And when she shows up to go to the monastery, it's like everything's gonna...

04:18:24.832 --> 04:18:24.972
Delwath: Yeah.

04:18:26.572 --> 04:18:26.812
DM: All right.

04:18:26.852 --> 04:18:27.232
Delwath: We need to-

04:18:27.592 --> 04:18:27.812
Seeker: Let's go.

04:18:27.812 --> 04:18:33.072
Delwath: We need to get in and out of Tokra quickly and be off fighting demons in the east when Dunmar falls into civil war.

04:18:34.851 --> 04:18:36.751
Seeker: That's an interesting plan.

04:18:38.472 --> 04:18:41.812
Wellby: At least we'll be a minor footnote in the historical record

04:18:42.872 --> 04:18:45.072
Wellby: as the cause of the great Dunmari civil war.

04:18:45.092 --> 04:18:46.272
Delwath: Yeah. [laughs]

04:18:46.272 --> 04:18:46.312
Seeker: Oh.

04:18:46.332 --> 04:18:47.092
Unknown: Fuck.

04:18:47.112 --> 04:18:55.372
Seeker: When... A, a minor footnote that someone suddenly leaps to a conclusion about when they discover the mirror that we're all trapped inside of and break it to release us again.

04:18:55.372 --> 04:18:56.092
Delwath: Yeah. [laughs]

04:18:56.132 --> 04:18:56.952
Seeker: Millennia hence.

04:18:58.232 --> 04:19:01.072
Wellby: Could we just ride this thing out in the mirror for a few centuries?

04:19:01.292 --> 04:19:01.352
Delwath: Oh, yeah.

04:19:01.352 --> 04:19:02.872
Seeker: That's what I'm talking about.

04:19:02.872 --> 04:19:03.812
Seeker: It'll all blow over.

04:19:05.852 --> 04:19:07.872
Delwath: Yeah, Delwath tried that. It didn't work that well.

04:19:08.692 --> 04:19:13.192
Delwath: Although I guess this is really kind of calm and nice, happy times compared to the great war.

04:19:13.572 --> 04:19:13.572
Seeker: Like

04:19:13.572 --> 04:19:15.572
Delwath: So maybe it worked really well, actually.

04:19:16.672 --> 04:19:21.112
DM: So in the interest of giving a moment to role play saying goodbye to Drikod,

04:19:22.292 --> 04:19:22.492
DM: um,

04:19:24.532 --> 04:19:30.952
DM: Kendrasa thanks you again and, and says, "I, I hope someday we may see you again in Karawa.

04:19:33.552 --> 04:19:34.872
DM: You are always welcome here."

04:19:37.532 --> 04:19:38.612
Unknown: We will certainly be back.

04:19:39.552 --> 04:19:40.612
Unknown: We'll certainly be back.

04:19:42.692 --> 04:19:45.632
DM: And he then looks specifically at, um,

04:19:46.772 --> 04:19:48.892
DM: at Kenzo and at Drikod and he says,

04:19:49.912 --> 04:19:50.292
DM: and he, like,

04:19:51.312 --> 04:19:57.132
DM: bows to you both and says, "And you will always be with me."

04:19:59.012 --> 04:19:59.932
Unknown: Always and forever.

04:20:02.032 --> 04:20:02.452
DM: Thank you.

04:20:02.452 --> 04:20:03.972
Kenzo: Thank, thank you, Kendrasa.

04:20:04.472 --> 04:20:04.952
Unknown: Thank you.

04:20:06.452 --> 04:20:12.152
Kenzo: Kenzo, Kenzo looks over at, at Drikod, kind of puts a hand to his, uh, to his face.

04:20:14.792 --> 04:20:15.312
Unknown: Drikod,

04:20:16.672 --> 04:20:17.772
Unknown: we will always be connected.

04:20:19.952 --> 04:20:20.432
Drikod: Yes.

04:20:21.272 --> 04:20:22.012
Drikod: We will always

04:20:23.352 --> 04:20:24.212
Drikod: feel her heart.

04:20:28.032 --> 04:20:30.332
Kenzo: How many days' travel to, to home for you?

04:20:32.212 --> 04:20:34.992
Drikod: Many days, but easy traveling.

04:20:34.992 --> 04:20:38.132
Drikod: Easier than what we have done the past few weeks.

04:20:39.992 --> 04:20:41.692
Drikod: I think the roads will be much safer now.

04:20:44.892 --> 04:20:45.171
Unknown: What is your-

04:20:45.231 --> 04:20:47.152
Drikod: I, I miss, I miss my villages.

04:20:47.152 --> 04:20:48.152
Drikod: I miss my people.

04:20:50.132 --> 04:20:51.772
Drikod: It's hot and dry here.

04:20:55.632 --> 04:20:57.112
Unknown: What is your plan upon your return home?

04:20:59.232 --> 04:21:00.572
Drikod: To smell the mountains.

04:21:01.212 --> 04:21:02.492
Drikod: To hear the snow.

04:21:03.932 --> 04:21:08.852
Drikod: To tell the, to tell the elders that we should be safe for a little longer.

04:21:10.232 --> 04:21:13.572
Drikod: The villages are more connected than we knew,

04:21:14.732 --> 04:21:17.832
Drikod: and what goes on outside of the mountain impacts us.

04:21:18.972 --> 04:21:20.592
Drikod: I imagine we'll be more involved.

04:21:23.392 --> 04:21:23.972
DM: Drikod.

04:21:23.992 --> 04:21:25.172
Unknown: Drikod. Oh.

04:21:25.212 --> 04:21:25.372
Drikod: Oh.

04:21:26.512 --> 04:21:27.812
Seeker: Should you need

04:21:28.752 --> 04:21:33.672
Seeker: to tell the stories of your adventures to the little ones of your village, perhaps this might be of help.

04:21:34.492 --> 04:21:37.332
Seeker: And I bring forth a, a tiny stone carving.

04:21:38.112 --> 04:21:38.252
Seeker: Uh,

04:21:39.232 --> 04:21:43.472
Seeker: I made this, uh, for you to help commemorate our adventures together.

04:21:43.472 --> 04:21:53.272
Seeker: And as you look closely, you see it's very small, but it is a faithful and perfectly detailed replica depicting not just any ax beak, but Baxter in particular.

04:21:53.272 --> 04:21:54.812
Drikod: [laughs]

04:21:54.812 --> 04:21:59.032
Seeker: And th- [laughs] And th- and then

04:21:59.032 --> 04:21:59.172
Drikod: So pretty

04:21:59.172 --> 04:21:59.972
Seeker: ... Seeker pulls out

04:22:01.012 --> 04:22:03.792
Seeker: a half dozen additional ones that are also identical replicas

04:22:03.792 --> 04:22:04.252
Drikod: [laughs]

04:22:04.252 --> 04:22:05.452
Seeker: ... of Baxter in particular.

04:22:05.452 --> 04:22:07.272
Drikod: [laughs]

04:22:07.292 --> 04:22:12.552
Seeker: And says, "Here, take these as a gift in remembrance from me of our time together."

04:22:12.632 --> 04:22:15.812
Drikod: Drikod carefully places them in a pouch, smiling.

04:22:16.612 --> 04:22:18.352
Drikod: The dwarves and the Stoneborn have

04:22:19.552 --> 04:22:21.372
Drikod: long history together.

04:22:22.912 --> 04:22:26.892
Drikod: Honestly, he kind of says, "You're the only one I kind of understand.

04:22:26.892 --> 04:22:28.792
Drikod: Everything else is really confusing."

04:22:28.792 --> 04:22:28.912
Drikod: [laughs]

04:22:32.540 --> 04:22:35.100
Drikod: [laughs] I don't know how they think or what they do what they do.

04:22:37.500 --> 04:22:42.080
Seeker: Perhaps the times ahead will hold a closer alliance between the dwarves and the Stoneborn.

04:22:49.280 --> 04:22:53.060
Wellby: Drikod, in, in two years I have an appointment in Sambara.

04:22:54.060 --> 04:22:59.440
Wellby: If I'm coming north from Dunmar, I hope I can stop in your village and see you again.

04:23:00.040 --> 04:23:02.500
Drikod: Yes, you are all welcome.

04:23:04.100 --> 04:23:08.760
Drikod: If you need safety or recovery or to hide,

04:23:09.660 --> 04:23:13.780
Drikod: the mountains are tall and large and isolated.

04:23:15.000 --> 04:23:15.960
Drikod: There is safety there.

04:23:16.440 --> 04:23:18.160
Wellby: And so are you, my friend.

04:23:18.160 --> 04:23:21.780
Wellby: [laughs]

04:23:21.780 --> 04:23:22.360
Unknown: [laughs] Nice.

04:23:24.640 --> 04:23:27.500
Delwath: It's been... Delwath will, will say, "It's been an honor,

04:23:28.520 --> 04:23:31.660
Delwath: uh, traveling with you and defeating

04:23:33.360 --> 04:23:38.340
Delwath: Agata together, and your offer of refuge in the mountain is

04:23:39.720 --> 04:23:40.680
Delwath: much appreciated.

04:23:41.620 --> 04:23:42.060
Delwath: If the,

04:23:43.360 --> 04:23:44.520
Delwath: if a new great war

04:23:45.800 --> 04:23:46.560
Delwath: starts and

04:23:48.180 --> 04:23:52.680
Delwath: it all falls apart, we may take you up on this, or I may, Delwath may take you up on this.

04:23:53.580 --> 04:23:53.740
Delwath: Um,

04:23:54.920 --> 04:23:58.460
Delwath: but I think there's more in the world to see for now."

04:24:01.180 --> 04:24:07.240
Kenzo: Drikod, in, in all great seriousness, um, since I've met this group,

04:24:08.700 --> 04:24:09.300
Unknown: I've felt

04:24:10.660 --> 04:24:12.360
Kenzo: internally a deep restlessness,

04:24:13.440 --> 04:24:17.080
Kenzo: a sense of lack of peace, a lack of calm.

04:24:18.900 --> 04:24:19.120
Unknown: Um,

04:24:21.080 --> 04:24:23.900
Kenzo: I think your offer of, of, of

04:24:24.920 --> 04:24:26.460
Kenzo: solace in the mountains, um,

04:24:27.540 --> 04:24:30.280
Kenzo: may be an offer that's taken sooner than later.

04:24:30.280 --> 04:24:30.940
Unknown: I think, um,

04:24:32.080 --> 04:24:34.380
Kenzo: the thought of Chardin, civil war in Dunmar,

04:24:35.280 --> 04:24:37.440
Kenzo: I'm not sure how much of this I can take, to be very honest.

04:24:38.460 --> 04:24:38.800
Unknown: So...

04:24:39.820 --> 04:24:44.200
Drikod: There, there are old gods in the mountains, an old power in the mountains.

04:24:46.120 --> 04:24:47.140
Drikod: There's much to learn.

04:24:49.440 --> 04:24:51.320
Kenzo: It's good to know that we have a brother, a brother there.

04:24:53.420 --> 04:24:54.180
Unknown: Until very soon.

04:24:58.120 --> 04:25:03.780
Drikod: Drikod lumbers away, walking north, right?

04:25:03.780 --> 04:25:04.300
Drikod: Yeah, we're north.

04:25:04.360 --> 04:25:04.560
DM: Yeah.

04:25:05.600 --> 04:25:16.120
DM: So as you all are leaving, you know, saying your goodbyes as you leave Carowa in the morning, Drikod heading north, the four of you heading west towards Tokra,

04:25:16.120 --> 04:25:19.580
DM: um, Sintra waves a last goodbye, Jumya at her side,

04:25:22.000 --> 04:25:26.140
DM: looking at you all in gratitude and thanks.

04:25:26.920 --> 04:25:27.180
DM: And

04:25:28.700 --> 04:25:36.920
DM: you can... She doesn't say anything, but you can sense maybe a little disappointment or sadness at your leaving, given how,

04:25:38.140 --> 04:25:38.280
DM: um,

04:25:39.280 --> 04:25:45.560
DM: important you were to her path back to, to Carowa.

04:25:45.560 --> 04:25:46.980
DM: But she c- she waves out to you.

04:25:46.980 --> 04:25:57.100
DM: She's the only one out here as you're all leaving together early in the morning, m- most other people having, after the two days of the festival, like there's the, there's

04:25:57.120 --> 04:26:02.420
DM: the party and then there's the day of rest, but most people then also need like a day of rest to recover from the day of rest.

04:26:03.160 --> 04:26:03.360
DM: Um,

04:26:06.080 --> 04:26:09.380
DM: she waves. "Shakun goes with you, my friends.

04:26:10.060 --> 04:26:10.540
DM: Be well,"

04:26:13.540 --> 04:26:14.480
DM: as you ride off.

04:26:17.280 --> 04:26:18.440
DM: And that is where we'll stop.
